window.DM={"cats":[{"en":"Lungs","nl":"Longen"},{"en":"ENT & Eyes","nl":"KNO & Ogen"},{"en":"Skin","nl":"Huid"},{"en":"Pain & Mobility","nl":"Pijn & Mobiliteit"},{"en":"Nerves & Brain","nl":"Zenuwen & Hersenen"},{"en":"Digestive","nl":"Spijsvertering"},{"en":"Heart & Circulation","nl":"Hart & Bloedsomloop"},{"en":"Autoimmune","nl":"Auto-immuun"},{"en":"Oncology (Adjunct)","nl":"Oncologie (aanvullend)"},{"en":"Veterinary","nl":"Diergeneeskunde"},{"en":"How-To & Safety","nl":"Handleiding & Veiligheid"}],"p":[{"t":"ARDS (adjunct, experimental)","tn":"ARDS (aanvullend, experimenteel)","c":0,"en":"Presents DMSO as a hospital-only, experimental add-on for acute respiratory distress, based on older case and animal research into its anti-inflammatory effects. Not intended for home use.","nl":"Experimentele, uitsluitend klinische aanvulling bij acuut longfalen, onderbouwd met oud dier- en casusonderzoek naar ontstekingsremming. Uitdrukkelijk niet voor thuisgebruik."},{"t":"Asthma","tn":"Astma","c":0,"en":"Covers cautious use of DMSO for asthma, either rubbed on the chest or inhaled in very weak form, to ease tightness alongside regular medication.","nl":"Voorzichtig gebruik bij astma: op de borst smeren of zeer verdund vernevelen om benauwdheid te verlichten, altijd naast de gewone medicatie.","d":["Topical 30–40% to chest (AM), optional back (PM).","Nebulise 1–3 drops in 10–20 ml isotonic saline (0.9% salt water); stop if irritation.","Do not replace prescribed inhalers."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Bronchiolitis & Asthma – DMSO Aerosol & Topical Protocol","tn":"Bronchiolitis & astma – DMSO-aerosol en huidtoepassing","c":0,"en":"Describes DMSO given as an aerosol or on the skin for bronchiolitis and asthma in children, framed around its anti-inflammatory and mucus-loosening role. Paediatric use needs medical oversight.","nl":"Gaat over DMSO als aerosol of huidmiddel bij bronchiolitis en astma bij kinderen, vanwege de ontstekingsremmende en slijmoplossende werking. Bij kinderen alleen onder medisch toezicht.","d":["TOPICAL FOR ASTHMA: Apply a DMSO lotion containing aloe vera juice and eucalyptus oil to the chest, around the nose, and on the forehead at night before sleep.","AEROSOL FOR BRONCHIOLITIS (medical setting): DMSO combined with antibiotic and anti-inflammatory drug as an aerosol spray — physician administered.","For ongoing asthma management: apply DMSO lotion to the chest and upper back once or twice daily. Use 50–60% DMSO in an aloe vera base.","Do not suddenly stop prescribed cortisone or bronchodilators — DMSO is introduced gradually alongside existing medication.","Ensure adequate hydration throughout the day — water is essential for respiratory health and reduces DMSO side effects."],"fr":"Nightly (topical for asthma); as prescribed (aerosol for acute bronchiolitis)"},{"t":"COPD","tn":"COPD","c":0,"en":"Outlines weak inhaled DMSO and chest rubs for COPD, said to help breathing and coughing up mucus, and to boost uptake of other inhaled medicines.","nl":"Bij COPD: verdund vernevelen en insmeren van de borst, bedoeld om ademen en ophoesten te vergemakkelijken en andere inhalatiemiddelen beter te laten werken.","d":["Nebulise 1–5 drops in 10–20 ml saline; monitor SpO₂.","Topical 30–50% to chest/back 1–2×/day.","Combine with rehab & smoking cessation."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Cystic fibrosis (adjunct)","tn":"Taaislijmziekte (aanvullend)","c":0,"en":"Mentions scattered reports of DMSO combined with saline or glutathione for cystic fibrosis; stresses that a doctor must supervise.","nl":"Noemt losse meldingen van DMSO samen met zoutoplossing of glutathion bij taaislijmziekte; medisch toezicht is volgens de pagina onmisbaar."},{"t":"Lung Abscess & Pneumonia – Antibiotic Adjunct","tn":"Longabces & longontsteking – aanvulling op antibiotica","c":0,"en":"Frames DMSO as a helper that strengthens antibiotics in lung abscess and pneumonia, citing Russian clinical work. Clinical setting only.","nl":"DMSO als versterker van antibiotica bij longabces en longontsteking, met verwijzing naar Russisch klinisch onderzoek. Alleen in een medische setting.","d":["DMSO-antibiotic combination for lung infections is administered under medical supervision — typically by inhalation or intravenous route.","Adding DMSO to antibiotic inhalants has been shown to partially overcome antibiotic resistance in tuberculosis and enhance antibiotic penetration in pneumonia.","Topical chest application of DMSO (30–50% to the chest and upper back) may provide an adjunctive anti-inflammatory effect during respiratory infections.","Nebulised DMSO: ultra-low concentration (a few drops in saline) only. Never nebulise essential oils or high concentrations."],"fr":"As directed by a physician for systemic protocols; topical chest application once daily"},{"t":"Pneumonia (adjunct)","tn":"Longontsteking (aanvullend)","c":0,"en":"Describes DMSO as a way to help inhaled antimicrobial drugs penetrate in pneumonia, always under supervision.","nl":"Bij longontsteking soms ingezet om vernevelde antimicrobiële middelen beter te laten doordringen; alleen onder begeleiding.","d":["Clinical oversight only: ≤1% DMSO in isotonic saline (0.9% salt water) with approved nebulised agents.","Monitor vitals; discontinue if adverse symptoms."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Post‑viral cough / bronchitis","tn":"Postvirale hoest / bronchitis","c":0,"en":"Suggests short trials of weak inhaled DMSO for lingering cough after a virus or bronchitis, with ordinary comfort measures tried first.","nl":"Voor aanhoudende hoest na een virus of bronchitis: korte proef met verdund vernevelen, maar eerst de gewone huismiddelen.","d":["Nebulise 1–2 drops DMSO in 10–15 ml saline once daily for 3–5 days.","Steam inhalation separately (no oils with DMSO)."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Pulmonary fibrosis (adjunct)","tn":"Longfibrose (aanvullend)","c":0,"en":"Notes anecdotal symptom relief in pulmonary fibrosis from very dilute oral and skin use, while keeping standard treatment.","nl":"Anekdotische klachtenverlichting bij longfibrose via sterk verdunde inname of huidgebruik; de reguliere behandeling blijft gewoon doorlopen.","d":["Oral ≤20%: ½–1 tsp in large glass of water after food (short trials).","Topical 30–50% to posterior ribs; avoid mucosa."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Wildfire smoke / toxic exposure (adjunct)","tn":"Bosbrandrook / blootstelling aan giftige stoffen (aanvullend)","c":0,"en":"Mentions supportive use for airway irritation after breathing in smoke or toxic fumes.","nl":"Ondersteuning voor geïrriteerde luchtwegen na het inademen van rook of giftige dampen.","d":["Nebulise ultra‑low % under guidance.","Topical chest 30–40% for comfort."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Cataracts (Adjunct)","tn":"Staar (aanvullend)","c":1,"en":"Covers medically administered DMSO eye drops or eye injections as an add-on for cataract and related eye conditions. Specialist territory.","nl":"Medisch toegediende oogdruppels of injecties met DMSO als aanvulling bij staar en verwante oogaandoeningen. Terrein voor de oogarts.","d":["For cataracts: one drop of DMSO solution applied directly onto the eyeball — medical supervision required.","A combined solution of 25mg DMSO with 2cc superoxide dismutase (SOD) applied once or twice daily has been used clinically.","For macular degeneration or traumatic uveitis: 5mg DMSO in 1cc normal saline placed retrobulbar under Tenon's capsule — ophthalmologist procedure only.","Never apply undiluted or high-concentration DMSO to the eyes without medical guidance.","Ophthalmic DMSO protocols must be directed and monitored by a qualified ophthalmologist."],"fr":"Once or twice daily — as directed by an ophthalmologist"},{"t":"Cavities & Oral Health – DMSO Mouthwash Protocol","tn":"Gaatjes & mondgezondheid – DMSO-mondspoeling","c":1,"en":"Describes a homemade mouthwash combining DMSO with hydrogen peroxide and aloe for gum disease, tooth infections and cavities.","nl":"Zelfgemaakt mondwater met DMSO, waterstofperoxide en aloë, bedoeld voor tandvleesproblemen, tandinfecties en gaatjes.","d":["MOUTHWASH RECIPE: Combine 3.5ml pharmaceutical-grade DMSO + 3.5ml 3% food-grade hydrogen peroxide + 7ml distilled water (or 50:50 water and preservative-free aloe vera gel juice).","Swish for 2–3 minutes twice daily. Do not swallow. Spit thoroughly.","For active tooth infection or gum disease: apply 1–2 drops of the mouthwash formula directly to the affected tooth or gum area with a cotton swab 3–4 times daily.","For cavity control (Vollmer’s personal use for her child): apply 80% DMSO directly to the cavity site. This is not for general use — consult a holistic dentist.","Brush teeth with remineralising toothpaste (baking soda + activated charcoal, or clay-based). Add boron, magnesium, and vitamin K2 supplements to support tooth and bone remineralisation.","See a biological/mercury-free dentist for any serious dental issues."],"fr":"Twice daily mouthwash; supplements daily"},{"t":"Dental Decay & Gum Conditions","tn":"Tandbederf & tandvleesproblemen","c":1,"en":"Discusses DMSO in dental practice for gum problems, deep decay reaching the nerve, and painful dry socket after extraction.","nl":"DMSO in de tandartspraktijk bij tandvleesklachten, cariës tot in de zenuw en een pijnlijke droge tandkas na trekken.","d":["For gum inflammation or periodontal conditions: apply DMSO (30–40%) directly to the gum tissue using a cotton swab or gauze. Allow to settle for 1–2 minutes before rinsing.","For decay that has reached the nerve: DMSO applied by a dental professional directly to the affected area to reduce infection and inflammation.","For dry socket: place a few drops of DMSO directly into the extraction socket. Provides rapid pain relief and accelerated healing when combined with other dry socket treatments.","For parotitis (inflamed salivary glands): DMSO combined with procaine has been used topically over the parotid gland area."],"fr":"As needed for acute pain; 2–3 times daily for healing protocols"},{"t":"Dry eye / ocular surface (adjunct)","tn":"Droge ogen / oogoppervlak (aanvullend)","c":1,"en":"For dry eye, only extremely weak, eye-safe preparations under a specialist's care are considered.","nl":"Bij droge ogen alleen zeer zwakke, oogvriendelijke preparaten en uitsluitend via een specialist.","d":["Ophthalmology‑prepared ≤3% isotonic drops; supervision essential."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"General Eye Problems – DMSO Eye Drop Protocol","tn":"Algemene oogklachten – DMSO-oogdruppels","c":1,"en":"Presents daily DMSO eye drops for a range of eye complaints, including declining vision and macular degeneration. Carries a medical caution.","nl":"Dagelijkse DMSO-oogdruppels voor uiteenlopende oogklachten zoals achteruitgang van het zicht en maculadegeneratie. Met medisch voorbehoud.","d":["Place 1 drop of 40% DMSO in each eye once daily using a clean eye dropper.","Expect a stinging sensation lasting 30–40 seconds after instillation — this is normal and harmless.","After the stinging, eyes typically feel fresh and more comfortable than before the drop.","Combine with 1 teaspoon of DMSO in juice daily (oral) for best results in systemic eye conditions.","Have an ophthalmologist examine eyes every 2–4 weeks to objectively track visual acuity changes."],"fr":"Once daily (eye drops + oral)"},{"t":"Glaucoma (Adjunct)","tn":"Glaucoom (aanvullend)","c":1,"en":"Frames DMSO as an eye-care add-on for glaucoma that may enhance glaucoma medicines and lower eye pressure, under an eye doctor.","nl":"Aanvulling bij glaucoom die oogdrukverlagers zou versterken en de druk zou verlagen; onder leiding van een oogarts.","d":["DMSO-SOD drops (25mg DMSO with 2cc SOD) applied once or twice daily have been used for glaucoma and cataract clearing.","DMSO potentiates standard glaucoma drops — discuss with your ophthalmologist whether combining DMSO with your current glaucoma medication is appropriate.","All ocular DMSO use must be directed by an ophthalmologist and coordinated with existing glaucoma treatment."],"fr":"As directed by ophthalmologist"},{"t":"Hearing loss (adjunct)","tn":"Gehoorverlies (aanvullend)","c":1,"en":"Notes that some combine DMSO with nutrients for hearing loss, with mixed evidence.","nl":"Sommigen combineren DMSO met voedingsstoffen bij gehoorverlies; het bewijs is wisselend."},{"t":"Macular Degeneration & Retinal Disease (Adjunct)","tn":"Maculadegeneratie & netvliesaandoeningen (aanvullend)","c":1,"en":"Covers DMSO as an add-on for macular degeneration, retinitis pigmentosa, macular swelling and trauma-related eye inflammation.","nl":"Aanvullende inzet bij maculadegeneratie, retinitis pigmentosa, vochtophoping in de macula en ontsteking na oogletsel.","d":["DMSO retrobulbar instillation (5mg in 1cc saline behind the equator): ophthalmologist procedure.","For macular degeneration alone: DMSO eye drops have been used without the retrobulbar injection.","Combined DMSO + SOD (superoxide dismutase) drops: 5mg of 2cc DMSO with 5mg of 2cc SOD for a 4cc solution, applied once or twice daily.","All ocular protocols must be directed by an ophthalmologist. Home application is not appropriate for retinal conditions."],"fr":"Once or twice daily under ophthalmologist direction"},{"t":"Middle Ear Infections in Children (Adjunct)","tn":"Middenoorontsteking bij kinderen (aanvullend)","c":1,"en":"Describes DMSO helping antibiotics reach the middle ear in children with recurring or hard-to-treat ear infections. Under a doctor.","nl":"DMSO om antibiotica beter in het middenoor te krijgen bij kinderen met terugkerende of hardnekkige oorontsteking. Via de arts.","d":["DMSO carries antibiotics across the tympanic membrane to reduce middle ear infections.","This is a medical procedure performed by an ENT specialist or paediatrician.","Antibiotic drops combined with low-concentration DMSO (10–20%) are instilled into the ear canal under professional direction.","Do not self-administer DMSO ear drops without medical guidance, particularly in children."],"fr":"As directed by a paediatrician or ENT specialist"},{"t":"Retinitis Pigmentosa (Adjunct)","tn":"Retinitis pigmentosa (aanvullend)","c":1,"en":"An add-on approach for retinitis pigmentosa, the progressive retinal disease that narrows side vision.","nl":"Aanvullende aanpak bij retinitis pigmentosa, de voortschrijdende netvliesziekte die het zijzicht vernauwt.","d":["DMSO ophthalmic drops or retrobulbar instillation under ophthalmologist direction.","The original case: a patient with hand motion-only vision in one eye recovered to 20/50 visual acuity within 3 months of DMSO treatment.","Of 50 patients in the University of Oregon study: 22 improved in visual acuity, 9 in visual fields, 5 in dark adaptation.","All ocular protocols for retinitis pigmentosa must be directed and monitored by an ophthalmologist."],"fr":"As directed by ophthalmologist"},{"t":"Rhinitis / seasonal allergies (adjunct)","tn":"Rinitis / hooikoorts (aanvullend)","c":1,"en":"Reports some relief of nasal irritation in hay fever from very weak use inside the nose.","nl":"Bij hooikoorts melden sommigen minder neusirritatie door zeer verdund gebruik in de neus.","d":["Intranasal ≤5% in isotonic saline (0.9% salt water) short trials; stop if stinging."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Sinusitis (adjunct)","tn":"Sinusitis (aanvullend)","c":1,"en":"Very dilute nasal solutions for sinusitis appear in some protocols; strong mixes on mucous membranes should be avoided.","nl":"Bij bijholteontsteking komen zeer verdunde neusoplossingen voor; sterke mengsels op slijmvlies zijn af te raden.","d":["Intranasal 5–10% in isotonic saline (0.9% salt water), 1–2 drops/nostril daily up to 3–5 days; stop if stinging.","Perinasal skin: 10–20% a very light layer (just enough to make the skin shiny, not wet); avoid eyes."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Sinusitis & Sinus Inflammation – DMSO Neti Pot Rinse","tn":"Sinusitis & bijholteontsteking – DMSO-neusspoeling (netipot)","c":1,"en":"Describes adding DMSO to a saline neti-pot rinse for acute or chronic sinus infections and allergy-related congestion.","nl":"DMSO toegevoegd aan een neusspoeling met zout water (neti pot) bij acute of chronische sinusitis en allergische klachten.","d":["Make a saline solution: 240ml (8 oz) lukewarm distilled water + ¼ tsp neti salt or non-iodised sea salt. Stir until dissolved. (If using tap water, boil for 3 minutes and cool to lukewarm first.)","Add 11ml of pharmaceutical-grade DMSO to the saline solution (creating approximately 5–10% DMSO).","Optionally add ½ teaspoon 15 ppm colloidal silver and/or ½ teaspoon preservative-free aloe vera gel juice.","Rinse both sinuses — even if only one side is affected. Always treat bilaterally.","If the rinse stings, add more aloe vera gel juice or reduce the DMSO volume.","Do not use if the inside of the nose is raw, bleeding, or has open sores."],"fr":"Once or twice daily for acute infection; once daily for maintenance"},{"t":"Stye / chalazion","tn":"Strontje / chalazion","c":1,"en":"For styes and chalazia, very weak application around the eyelid together with warm compresses.","nl":"Bij een strontje of hagelkorrel: zeer zwak rond het ooglid aanbrengen, samen met warme kompressen.","d":["Peri‑lid 5–10% using cotton tip; avoid ocular surface.","Warm compresses are first‑line."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Tinnitus – DMSO Ear Drop Protocol","tn":"Tinnitus – DMSO-oordruppels","c":1,"en":"Covers ear drops combining DMSO with anti-inflammatory and blood-vessel-widening drugs for tinnitus; prescription medicines are involved.","nl":"Oordruppels waarin DMSO wordt gecombineerd met ontstekingsremmers en vaatverwijders tegen oorsuizen; er zijn receptmiddelen bij betrokken.","d":["Place 2 drops of 40% DMSO in each ear daily using an eye dropper or dropper bottle.","Additionally, apply a lotion containing 90% DMSO, capsicum, and aloe vera around each ear twice daily.","For medical protocols: DMSO spray combined with anti-inflammatory and vasodilatory drugs in the ear canal every 4 days, plus daily intramuscular DMSO injection — physician administration.","Continue for at least 1 month — most patients achieve full relief within this period.","If symptoms return after stopping treatment, repeat the protocol — relief is typically faster on retreatment."],"fr":"Daily ear drops; twice daily external lotion"},{"t":"Tinnitus (adjunct)","tn":"Tinnitus (aanvullend)","c":1,"en":"Mentions applications around the ear for tinnitus comfort, with responses differing from person to person.","nl":"Aanbrengen rondom het oor bij oorsuizen; het effect verschilt sterk per persoon.","d":["Topical 25–35% behind ear 1× daily; avoid ear canal.","Trial 1–2 weeks."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Acne (adjunct)","tn":"Acne (aanvullend)","c":2,"en":"Positions DMSO as an add-on for acne, alone or with other agents, with a warning to watch for skin drying.","nl":"DMSO als aanvulling bij acne, los of met andere middelen; let op uitdroging van de huid.","d":["3% H₂O₂ cleanse","30–50% DMSO once daily; or 20–30% DMSO then chlorine dioxide solution (CDS)."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Anti-Ageing & Scar Healing – DMSO 40% Facial Protocol","tn":"Anti-veroudering & littekenherstel – DMSO 40% gezichtsbehandeling","c":2,"en":"Describes a DMSO and aloe vera face gel aimed at wrinkles, scars and acne, stressing the right strength for facial skin.","nl":"Gezichtsgel van DMSO en aloë tegen rimpels, littekens en acne, met nadruk op de juiste sterkte voor de gevoelige gezichtshuid.","d":["Cleanse the face completely with a natural, toxin-free cleanser. Remove all makeup and residue.","Apply a 40% DMSO solution in distilled water or preservative-free aloe vera gel juice to the face.","Allow 20 minutes to fully absorb before applying any other products or makeup.","If any film remains after 20 minutes, rinse with warm water and pat dry before applying makeup.","For small wounds, pimples, or scar tissue: 99.995% DMSO (full strength) can be applied sparingly to specific spots. Do not repeat on the same area daily."],"fr":"Once daily (morning or evening)"},{"t":"Burns (intact)","tn":"Brandwonden (intacte huid)","c":2,"en":"Covers sprays or solutions for comfort on burns where the skin is unbroken, under supervision.","nl":"Sprays of oplossingen voor verlichting bij brandwonden met intacte huid, onder begeleiding.","d":["Topical 20–50% thin spray/paint; monitor skin."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Chronic ulcers / diabetic foot (adjunct)","tn":"Chronische wonden / diabetische voet (aanvullend)","c":2,"en":"Describes improved healing of chronic and diabetic foot ulcers when DMSO is used alongside proper wound care.","nl":"Betere genezing van chronische en diabetische voetwonden gemeld wanneer DMSO naast goede wondzorg wordt gebruikt.","d":["20–50% post‑cleanse; 3× weekly to daily; off‑loading & glucose control."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Club Nails (Overgrown / Deformed Toenails)","tn":"Kalknagels (verdikte / misvormde teennagels)","c":2,"en":"Covers softening badly thickened, misshapen toenails with DMSO mixed with castor or olive oil.","nl":"Het verzachten van sterk verdikte, vervormde teennagels met DMSO gemengd met ricinus- of olijfolie.","d":["Combine 90% DMSO with castor oil or warm olive oil in equal parts.","Rub the oil-DMSO mixture thoroughly onto the club nail, working it into the nail root and nail grooves.","Allow to soak for 10–15 minutes — the nail softens and sensitivity at the root reduces.","Cut the nails with strong nail clippers. Smooth all rough edges with a nail file.","After trimming, paint the nails with the DMSO-oil mixture again to restore the compressed nail groove tissue.","Repeat before each nail trimming session. Apply DMSO-oil mixture between sessions to prevent excessive hardening."],"fr":"Before each trimming session; between sessions every 2–3 days"},{"t":"Cold sores (adjunct)","tn":"Koortslippen (aanvullend)","c":2,"en":"Refers to the herpes entry: DMSO used as a carrier for antiviral creams on cold sores.","nl":"Verwijst naar herpes: DMSO als drager voor antivirale crèmes bij koortslip.","d":["50–70% to lesion margins 2–3×/day; per label."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Eczema / atopic dermatitis (cautious)","tn":"Eczeem / atopische dermatitis (voorzichtig)","c":2,"en":"For eczema, only weak DMSO on unbroken skin is considered, with moisturisers remaining the first choice.","nl":"Bij eczeem hooguit zwak DMSO op onbeschadigde huid; vette crèmes blijven de eerste keus.","d":["3–10% patch‑tested every other day; stop if flare."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Fungal Toenails – DMSO + Antifungal Protocol","tn":"Schimmelnagels – DMSO + schimmelwerend middel","c":2,"en":"Describes DMSO carrying an antifungal drug into infected toenails as a paste. Involves a prescription antifungal.","nl":"DMSO als drager die een schimmeldodend middel in aangetaste teennagels brengt, als pasta. Er is een receptmiddel bij betrokken.","d":["After nail removal or filing by a podiatrist: prepare a paste of 30cc of 90% DMSO liquid with two 250mg microsize griseofulvin tablets, ground to powder.","Spread the paste into the nail matrix (growth area) after the nail bed has healed.","Cover with an adhesive strip to hold in contact. Replace the dressing and paste daily.","New, uninfected nail should appear from under the flesh within 2 months.","Continue the paste treatment for the full time it takes the new nail to grow over the nail bed — approximately 6 months.","Alternative: mix other liquid antifungal agents with DMSO and paint onto the healed nail bed; form a puddle under the flesh flap over the nail growth centre; cover with plastic tape."],"fr":"Daily until new nail fully grows (approximately 6 months)"},{"t":"Hair Loss & Scalp Problems","tn":"Haaruitval & hoofdhuidproblemen","c":2,"en":"Covers a scalp lotion with DMSO claimed to encourage hair growth and treat scalp infections.","nl":"Hoofdhuidlotion met DMSO die haargroei zou stimuleren en hoofdhuidinfecties zou aanpakken.","d":["Apply a DMSO lotion (containing aloe vera and optionally a gentle herbal extract) to the scalp once or twice daily.","Massage gently into the scalp, focusing on areas of thinning or loss.","For post-chemotherapy hair regrowth: begin as soon as chemotherapy ends. Hair regrowth was much faster than expected in documented cases.","For scalp infections: apply a DMSO lotion directly to the infected scalp area twice daily. Continue for 2–3 weeks beyond full symptom resolution.","For hair colour preservation: long-term regular use (daily or every other day) has been associated with maintained hair colour."],"fr":"Once or twice daily"},{"t":"Ingrown Toenails","tn":"Ingegroeide teennagels","c":2,"en":"For early ingrown toenails, a tiny amount on the inflamed nail fold is said to calm swelling quickly.","nl":"Bij een beginnende ingegroeide teennagel: een heel klein beetje op de ontstoken nagelwal zou de zwelling snel afremmen.","d":["For early-stage ingrown toenail (inflammation, mild discomfort, no pus): clean the toe thoroughly and place 1–2 drops of 50–70% DMSO directly onto the inflamed nail groove.","Allow to absorb fully before putting on socks or footwear.","Repeat once or twice daily while symptoms persist.","If infection has developed (pus, significant swelling, red streaks on the foot): seek podiatric care immediately — DMSO alone is not sufficient and antibiotics may be required.","Prevent recurrence by cutting toenails straight across — never rounded."],"fr":"Once or twice daily for early-stage cases"},{"t":"Jungle Rot & Chronic Resistant Fungal Skin Infections","tn":"Tropische voetschimmel & hardnekkige schimmelinfecties van de huid","c":2,"en":"Describes a DMSO and aloe lotion for stubborn, long-lasting fungal skin infections such as tropical \"jungle rot\".","nl":"Lotion van DMSO en aloë voor hardnekkige, langdurige schimmelinfecties van de huid, zoals tropische 'jungle rot'.","d":["Apply a skin lotion containing 70–90% DMSO and aloe vera juice directly to the infected skin area.","Apply twice daily — morning and evening.","For athlete’s foot: apply DMSO at 50–90% concentration directly to affected skin; optionally mix with capsicum pepper and aloe vera.","Allow shoes to thoroughly dry and air out between wearings — ongoing shoe hygiene is essential to prevent reinfection.","Continue treatment during warm seasons or whenever conditions favour fungal regrowth. Long-term use may be necessary."],"fr":"Twice daily; ongoing during risk periods"},{"t":"Keloids / hypertrophic scars (adjunct)","tn":"Keloïden / hypertrofische littekens (aanvullend)","c":2,"en":"An add-on to silicone and pressure therapy for keloids and raised scars; results vary.","nl":"Aanvulling op siliconen en druktherapie bij keloïd en verdikte littekens; resultaten wisselen.","d":["30–50% a very light layer (just enough to make the skin shiny, not wet) once daily; combine with silicone/pressure."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Mature scars / adhesions","tn":"Oude littekens / verklevingen","c":2,"en":"Describes stronger application on old, settled scars and adhesions to make the tissue more supple.","nl":"Sterkere toepassing op oude, uitgerijpte littekens en verklevingen om het weefsel soepeler te maken.","d":["40–70% to mature scar once daily–twice daily (morning and evening) × 4–12 weeks."],"fr":"Twice daily"},{"t":"Molluscum contagiosum (adjunct)","tn":"Molluscum contagiosum (waterwratjes, aanvullend)","c":2,"en":"Notes occasional reported use on molluscum lesions.","nl":"Af en toe gemeld gebruik op waterwratjes (molluscum).","d":["20–40% focal application; monitor irritation."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Onychomycosis (fungal nail) adjunct","tn":"Onychomycose (nagelschimmel), aanvullend","c":2,"en":"Frames DMSO as helping antifungal medicines penetrate the nail plate in fungal nail infection.","nl":"DMSO als hulpmiddel om schimmelmiddelen door de nagelplaat te laten dringen bij kalknagels.","d":["30–50% to nail after filing; plus antifungal."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Perioral dermatitis (cautious)","tn":"Periorale dermatitis (voorzichtig)","c":2,"en":"For perioral dermatitis, only weak use and avoidance of known triggers.","nl":"Bij rode, schilferige huid rond de mond alleen zwak gebruiken en bekende triggers vermijden.","d":["3–10% spot application; gentle skincare."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Pressure Ulcers (Bed Sores) – DMSO Early Intervention","tn":"Doorligwonden (decubitus) – vroege behandeling met DMSO","c":2,"en":"Covers applying DMSO early to prevent bed sores forming and to speed healing of existing ones.","nl":"Vroegtijdig aanbrengen om doorligwonden te voorkomen en bestaande sneller te laten genezen.","d":["PREVENTION: Apply a 40–50% DMSO solution to skin over high-risk pressure areas (heels, sacrum, hips, shoulders) twice daily.","For EARLY-STAGE ulcers (redness, warmth, without open skin): apply 50% DMSO with preservative-free aloe vera 2–3 times daily. This can halt progression entirely.","For ESTABLISHED ulcers: apply DMSO to the wound edge and surrounding area (not directly into the open wound if deeply infected). DMSO promotes blood flow to the wound bed and supports tissue repair.","Pair with colloidal silver spray to the wound surface for antibacterial protection.","Position changes every 2 hours remain essential — DMSO is an adjunct to, not a replacement for, pressure relief."],"fr":"2–3 times daily"},{"t":"Psoriasis (adjunct)","tn":"Psoriasis (aanvullend)","c":2,"en":"Describes variable results in psoriasis, sometimes using DMSO to carry plant-based remedies.","nl":"Wisselende resultaten bij psoriasis; DMSO dient soms als drager voor plantaardige middelen.","d":["10–30% once daily over plaques, 2–8 weeks; reassess."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Radiation dermatitis (intact skin)","tn":"Bestralingsdermatitis (intacte huid)","c":2,"en":"Comfort support for skin affected by radiotherapy, only where unbroken and with the treatment team's approval.","nl":"Verzachting van door bestraling aangetaste huid, alleen bij intacte huid en met instemming van het behandelteam.","d":["10–30% a very light layer (just enough to make the skin shiny, not wet) 1–2×/day; coordinate with oncology."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Rosacea (cautious)","tn":"Rosacea (voorzichtig)","c":2,"en":"Warns that many rosacea sufferers are sensitive; only very weak use after a test patch.","nl":"Mensen met rosacea zijn vaak gevoelig; alleen heel zwak en na een testplekje.","d":["3–10% patch‑tested; stop if flushing/irritation."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Seborrhoeic dermatitis","tn":"Seborroïsch eczeem","c":2,"en":"For seborrhoeic dermatitis, very weak use on small areas together with antifungals.","nl":"Bij seborroïsch eczeem zeer verdund op kleine plekken, samen met schimmelwerende middelen.","d":["3–10% to small patches once daily for 2–4 weeks."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Sunburn (adjunct)","tn":"Zonnebrand (aanvullend)","c":2,"en":"Reports a cooling, soothing effect on sunburn.","nl":"Gemeld als verkoelend en verzachtend bij zonnebrand.","d":["20–40% a very light layer (just enough to make the skin shiny, not wet); moisturise after drying."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Tinea (fungal skin) adjunct","tn":"Tinea (huidschimmel), aanvullend","c":2,"en":"Frames DMSO as improving the penetration of antifungals in fungal skin infections.","nl":"Verbetert volgens de pagina de opname van schimmelmiddelen bij huidschimmel.","d":["20–40% with antifungal cream."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Varicose ulcers (adjunct)","tn":"Open been / spataderzweren (aanvullend)","c":2,"en":"Support for pain and healing of venous leg ulcers alongside compression therapy.","nl":"Ondersteuning bij pijn en genezing van open benen door spataderen, naast compressietherapie.","d":["20–50% to peri‑wound; avoid bleeding surfaces; compression."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Warts / viral lesions","tn":"Wratten / virale huidletsels","c":2,"en":"Describes focused stronger applications on warts, with neighbouring skin protected.","nl":"Gerichte, sterkere toepassing op wratten, waarbij de omliggende huid beschermd wordt.","d":["50–75% point‑apply once daily; barrier ointment; short contact then rinse."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Achilles & Ankles – DMSO Routine","tn":"Achillespees & enkels – DMSO-routine","c":3,"en":"A targeted routine along the Achilles tendon and ankle, following the line from heel to calf.","nl":"Gerichte routine voor achillespees en enkel, van de hiel omhoog richting kuit.","d":["Position the foot so the back of the ankle is easy to reach — rest it on a low stool or extend the leg with the heel slightly raised.","Clean the skin — socks and shoes leave behind fibres, sweat, and residue.","Apply a thin layer of DMSO along the Achilles from heel toward the lower calf using a roll-on.","If the sides of the ankle feel involved, trace the curve around the bone; use a spray for broader coverage.","Allow to air-dry fully with the foot relaxed before the foot bends again.","Optionally apply a warm cloth if the tendon feels stiff; a cool cloth after long periods of standing or activity."],"fr":"Daily or after prolonged standing and activity"},{"t":"Achilles tendinopathy","tn":"Achillespeesklachten (tendinopathie)","c":3,"en":"Topical support for Achilles tendon problems, combined with heel-drop strengthening exercises.","nl":"Ondersteuning bij achillespeesklachten, gecombineerd met krachtoefeningen voor de kuit.","d":["50–90% once daily × 3–6 weeks."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Acute sprains / strains","tn":"Acute verstuikingen / verrekkingen","c":3,"en":"For fresh sprains and strains, framed as easing pain and swelling and speeding recovery when paired with rehab.","nl":"Bij verstuikingen en verrekkingen: minder pijn en zwelling en sneller herstel, mits samen met revalidatie.","d":["50–90% to injured area once daily–twice daily (morning and evening) × 3–7 days."],"fr":"Twice daily"},{"t":"Arthritis – DMSO + MSM Joint Gel Protocol","tn":"Artritis – DMSO + MSM gewrichtsgel","c":3,"en":"A joint protocol layering DMSO with an MSM gel for arthritic and rheumatic joints.","nl":"Gewrichtsprotocol waarbij DMSO en een MSM-gel in lagen worden aangebracht bij artrose en reuma.","d":["Cleanse the area thoroughly, removing all soap, sweat, or lotion residues.","Apply a very thin layer of DMSO over the joint using a spray or roll-on — aim for an even film, not a heavy coat.","Wait 1–2 minutes for the DMSO to settle.","Gently apply a small amount of MSM gel on top as a finishing layer.","Introduce gentle mobility: slow bends, small rotations, light hand opening/closing, easy weight shifting for knees or hips.","Wear clean, loose cotton clothing over the joint afterward to prevent friction."],"fr":"Once or twice daily"},{"t":"Arthritis – Mobility & Cartilage Support","tn":"Artritis – ondersteuning van beweeglijkheid & kraakbeen","c":3,"en":"A skin routine aimed at the grinding, dry-friction feeling in arthritic joints and better joint glide.","nl":"Huidroutine tegen het stroeve, schurende gevoel in artrotische gewrichten, voor soepeler bewegen.","d":["Cleanse the skin around the joint and apply a light, even layer of your DMSO blend.","Allow it to settle for 1–2 minutes.","Optionally warm the area beforehand with a brief warm cloth or shower if the joint feels rigid; use a cooling moment first if the joint feels puffy or warm.","Introduce small, gentle movements: slow bends and extensions, small circles, light hand opening/closing, or gentle weight shifting for knees and hips.","Layer MSM gel or aloe vera on top once DMSO has dried.","Apply before activities that require mobility — walking, housework, gardening — to prime the joint."],"fr":"Daily, ideally before activity"},{"t":"Arthritis – Reducing Joint Inflammation","tn":"Artritis – gewrichtsontsteking verminderen","c":3,"en":"A morning and evening routine to calm stiffness, warmth and swelling in inflamed arthritic joints.","nl":"Ochtend- en avondroutine om stijfheid, warmte en zwelling in ontstoken gewrichten te temperen.","d":["Gently wash the affected joint with warm water and an unscented cleanser; pat completely dry.","Apply a thin, even layer of DMSO blend directly over the joint — use a spray for knees, hips, or shoulders; a roll-on or fingertip for fingers and wrists.","Allow the product to settle for 2–3 minutes without rubbing.","Layer aloe vera gel, magnesium oil, or MSM gel on top once DMSO has dried.","Introduce gentle mobility: open and close the hand, bend and extend the knee, or rotate the shoulder in small circles.","For swollen or warm joints, finish with a cool compress. For rigid or locked joints, use a warm cloth instead.","Repeat morning and evening for best results."],"fr":"Twice daily — morning and evening"},{"t":"Back Pain & Sciatica – DMSO + Magnesium Oil Blend","tn":"Rugpijn & ischias – DMSO + magnesiumolie","c":3,"en":"Combines DMSO with magnesium oil on the skin for tight backs, sciatica-type pain and stubborn muscle tension.","nl":"DMSO met magnesiumolie op de huid bij een stijve rug, ischiasachtige pijn en hardnekkige spierspanning.","d":["Rinse or warm the skin with a cloth — this reduces any tingling from the magnesium oil.","Apply a light layer of DMSO first; allow 1–2 minutes to settle.","Apply a small amount of magnesium oil on top (a few sprays or a quick rub).","If magnesium feels too intense, add a small amount of aloe vera or dab lightly with a damp cloth.","Optionally trace a thin strip from the lower back toward the hip, concentrating where the sensation is strongest.","Introduce slow movement: gentle hip shifting, easy shoulder rolls, light knee bends, or ankle flexing.","Once dry, place a clean cotton cloth or warm compress over the area. Ideal timing: 45–60 minutes before bed."],"fr":"Once daily — preferably in the evening"},{"t":"Back Pain, Sciatica & Disc Injury – Topical & Compress","tn":"Rugpijn, ischias & hernia – huidtoepassing & kompres","c":3,"en":"Skin application plus compresses for low back pain, sciatica-like symptoms and disc-related stiffness.","nl":"Insmeren en kompressen bij lage rugpijn, ischiasklachten en stijfheid door een hernia.","d":["Cleanse the lower back with warm water or a brief shower to remove sweat, fabric residues, and lotion.","For broad lumbar pain, apply DMSO blend with a spray for wide coverage without awkward twisting.","For sciatic-type pain tracing toward the hip, use a roll-on to follow the sensation pathway precisely.","Allow the product to settle without rubbing.","For stiff or locked back: place a warm, well-wrung cotton cloth over the treated area for 5–10 minutes.","For a warm, puffy, or irritated back: use a cool cloth instead.","Lie slightly on your side with a pillow between the knees during compress time.","Use before triggering activities (lifting, long drives) and after to release accumulated tension."],"fr":"As needed — ideally before and after activity"},{"t":"Bunions (Hallux Valgus & Acute Bursitis)","tn":"Hallux valgus (knokkel) & acute slijmbeursontsteking","c":3,"en":"Topical use on the big-toe joint to calm bunion inflammation and bursitis.","nl":"Aanbrengen op het grote-teengewricht om ontsteking bij een hallux valgus en slijmbeursontsteking te remmen.","d":["Cleanse the big toe and foot thoroughly — remove any lotion, sock fibres, or residue.","Paint 70–80% DMSO directly onto the inflamed bunion area.","Optionally cover with an impervious plastic wrap held in place with felt padding and supportive strapping for sustained contact.","Leave in place for several hours, or until pain relief is established. Re-examine skin condition regularly.","Reapply every 4–6 hours as needed for acute flare-ups.","After 12 hours of intensive treatment, remove dressings, wash the foot, and apply aloe vera or a soothing moisturiser."],"fr":"Every 4–6 hours during acute flare; once daily for ongoing management"},{"t":"Bursitis – DMSO 80% Topical Protocol","tn":"Slijmbeursontsteking – DMSO 80% op de huid","c":3,"en":"Strong topical DMSO over inflamed bursae in shoulder, hip, elbow or knee, with long-term regular use described.","nl":"Sterk DMSO op ontstoken slijmbeurzen in schouder, heup, elleboog of knie, met nadruk op langdurig volhouden.","d":["Apply 5ml of 80% DMSO solution to the inflamed bursae and well beyond the immediate area, 2–4 times daily.","Leave the solution on the skin for 20 minutes, then wipe off any residue.","Follow each application with 10–15 sprays of topical magnesium oil over the same area to help dissolve calcium deposits.","Apply vitamin C castor oil packs (wool flannel soaked in castor oil, laid over the joint with a hot water bottle for 20 minutes) once daily.","Continue consistently for several months for chronic bursitis. Acute bursitis may resolve much faster."],"fr":"2–4 times daily"},{"t":"Carpal tunnel (adjunct)","tn":"Carpaletunnelsyndroom (aanvullend)","c":3,"en":"Short-term symptom relief for carpal tunnel, alongside a wrist splint and better ergonomics.","nl":"Tijdelijke verlichting bij carpaletunnelsyndroom, naast een polsspalk en een betere werkhouding.","d":["40–60% to volar wrist once daily; night splint."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Cervical tension / neck pain","tn":"Nekspanning / nekpijn","c":3,"en":"Neck pain and tension support, usually combined with gentle mobility exercises.","nl":"Bij nekpijn en spanning, meestal samen met rustige bewegingsoefeningen.","d":["30–50% to cervical paraspinals once daily; posture/mobility."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Chronic Pain – Nighttime Relief Routine","tn":"Chronische pijn – verlichting voor de nacht","c":3,"en":"A bedtime routine aimed at easing persistent pain from old injuries, stiffness and deep muscle tension.","nl":"Routine voor het slapengaan tegen aanhoudende pijn door oude blessures, stijfheid en diepe spierspanning.","d":["45–60 minutes before bed, apply DMSO blend to areas that consistently disrupt sleep: lower back, knees, hands, or tops of the feet.","For sensitive, warm, or irritated areas (knees with weather-related ache, reactive hands): use an aloe-based DMSO blend for a cooling, buffering effect.","For muscular pain with strong tension (tight hamstrings, cramping calves, stiff shoulders): use a magnesium + DMSO blend.","Allow to absorb fully, then place a warm or cool compress over the area depending on what feels most soothing.","For feet and calves, apply magnesium + DMSO and allow to absorb fully before sleep."],"fr":"Nightly — 45–60 minutes before bed"},{"t":"Contusions / haematoma","tn":"Kneuzingen / blauwe plekken (hematoom)","c":3,"en":"Reported to soothe bruises and help them clear faster.","nl":"Zou kneuzingen en bloeduitstortingen verzachten en sneller laten wegtrekken.","d":["40–70% to area once daily; rest/ice as needed."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Costochondritis","tn":"Ontsteking van het borstbeenkraakbeen (costochondritis)","c":3,"en":"Soothing application over the tender rib-cartilage joints in costochondritis.","nl":"Verzachtend aanbrengen op de pijnlijke overgang van rib naar borstbeen (syndroom van Tietze).","d":["40–70% a very light layer (just enough to make the skin shiny, not wet) once daily × 1–2 weeks."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"CRPS (adjunct)","tn":"CRPS (aanvullend)","c":3,"en":"Explored for nerve pain and skin changes in complex regional pain syndrome; results vary.","nl":"Onderzocht bij zenuwpijn en huidveranderingen bij CRPS (posttraumatische dystrofie); wisselende uitkomsten.","d":["50–90% to affected area 2–3×/day; tiny test area first."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Dislocations – Post-Reduction Recovery","tn":"Ontwrichtingen – herstel na terugzetten","c":3,"en":"Use after a dislocated joint has been put back, to reduce leftover pain and swelling.","nl":"Na het terugzetten van een ontwricht gewricht, om resterende pijn en zwelling te verminderen.","d":["Ensure the dislocation has been medically assessed and properly reduced before applying DMSO.","Cleanse the skin around the joint thoroughly.","Apply 50–70% DMSO to the entire joint area using a spray or roll-on — cover the joint capsule and surrounding muscles.","Allow to dry fully before covering with a support or compression bandage.","Apply twice daily for the first 3–5 days post-reduction to manage swelling and pain.","Reduce frequency to once daily once acute swelling has subsided."],"fr":"Twice daily for 3–5 days; then once daily"},{"t":"Elbow – Tendon Support","tn":"Elleboog – ondersteuning van de pezen","c":3,"en":"An elbow routine following the tendon lines on the outer and inner sides of the joint.","nl":"Elleboogroutine langs de peeslijnen aan de buiten- en binnenkant van het gewricht.","d":["Rest the forearm on a table or across the lap with the elbow slightly bent.","Clean the skin — the elbow collects sweat, fabric residue, and product traces from handwashing.","Apply DMSO blend using slow strokes along the outer ridge of the elbow, the inner crease, and the upper forearm.","Use a roll-on to trace tendon pathways with precision; or a spray for broader elbow coverage.","Allow to air-dry with the elbow still for a moment to keep the layer even.","Optionally wrap a warm cloth around the joint if it feels tight, or a cool cloth if the area feels overworked."],"fr":"As needed — daily for chronic elbow strain"},{"t":"Fallen Arches (Pes Planus)","tn":"Platvoeten (pes planus)","c":3,"en":"DMSO combined with ultrasound as the first step of a podiatry approach to flat feet.","nl":"DMSO met ultrageluid als eerste stap in een podotherapeutische aanpak van platvoeten.","d":["Apply 50–70% DMSO to the entire arch area, inner ankle, and lower calf — the regions where fallen arch strain accumulates.","Optionally use DMSO as the coupling agent with ultrasound treatment (instead of standard ultrasound gel) for deeper tissue penetration.","Allow DMSO to dry fully, then apply a corrective supportive strapping.","Wear orthotic arch supports in all footwear as the ongoing corrective measure.","Use once daily during acute painful periods; reduce frequency to 3 times per week for maintenance."],"fr":"Daily during acute pain; 3 times per week for maintenance"},{"t":"Fibromyalgia – Herbal Anti-Inflammatory Synergy","tn":"Fibromyalgie – ontstekingsremmende kruidencombinatie","c":3,"en":"Layers DMSO with herbal preparations such as arnica or turmeric for broader relief in fibromyalgia.","nl":"DMSO in lagen met kruidenpreparaten als arnica of kurkuma voor bredere verlichting bij fibromyalgie.","d":["Cleanse the skin thoroughly.","Apply a thin layer of DMSO and allow to settle for 1–2 minutes.","Apply an herbal gel, balm, or oil on top: arnica gel for a cooling sensation; turmeric or boswellia cream for warmth over tight or achy areas.","For heightened sensitivity, choose lighter textures — aloe-based gels or diluted herbal oils — rather than thick balms.","For nerve pathway targeting, apply DMSO along the outer thigh, then arnica gel near the hip, then introduce gentle movement.","During flares (stress, weather changes, fatigue), layer DMSO with calming preparations such as chamomile or lavender oil."],"fr":"Once or twice daily — especially before activities that provoke discomfort"},{"t":"Fibromyalgia – Nervous System Support","tn":"Fibromyalgie – ondersteuning van het zenuwstelsel","c":3,"en":"Frames topical DMSO as calming overactive nerves in fibromyalgia and chronic pain.","nl":"Presenteert DMSO op de huid als middel om overprikkelde zenuwen te kalmeren bij fibromyalgie en chronische pijn.","d":["Begin with areas of highest skin tolerance (e.g., lower neck or shoulders) rather than the most painful spot.","Apply a thin layer of DMSO using a roll-on or spray to avoid unnecessary pressure on sensitive tissue.","Allow to settle without rubbing — common sensations include gentle warming, a spreading calm, or reduced surface sensitivity.","For burning or tingling nerve sensations, trace the product along the pathway: down the arm, along the outer thigh, or across the upper back.","After the DMSO dries, introduce small movements — shoulder rolls, neck tilts, light hand opening — to reinforce the settling sensation.","Apply before predictable flare periods: upon waking, during weather changes, after stress, or in the evening when fatigue sets in.","Wear soft, loose cotton clothing over treated areas after application."],"fr":"As needed — particularly at predictable flare times"},{"t":"Fracture Recovery – DMSO Adjunct","tn":"Herstel na botbreuk – DMSO als aanvulling","c":3,"en":"Topical use after a fracture has been immobilised, to reduce swelling and help regain movement.","nl":"Na het fixeren van een botbreuk aanbrengen om zwelling te beperken en de beweeglijkheid terug te winnen.","d":["DMSO is applied after the fracture has been medically stabilised (cast, splint, or surgical fixation) — not during acute fracture management.","Once the cast or immobilisation is removed: apply 50–70% DMSO to the affected area twice daily.","For ankle/foot fractures: apply to the entire foot and lower leg using a spray; allow to dry; then do gentle range-of-motion exercises.","For upper limb fractures: apply via roll-on to the joint and surrounding muscles; follow with slow, controlled movement.","For open fracture sites or surgical wounds: do not apply directly over healing incisions. Apply around the wound margin only."],"fr":"Twice daily after cast removal until full mobility is restored"},{"t":"Frozen shoulder (adhesive capsulitis)","tn":"Frozen shoulder (adhesieve capsulitis)","c":3,"en":"Support for frozen shoulder during range-of-motion rehab; progress is described as slow.","nl":"Ondersteuning bij een frozen shoulder tijdens bewegingsrevalidatie; vooruitgang gaat langzaam.","d":["40–70% around shoulder once daily; daily stretching."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Frozen Shoulder (Adhesive Capsulitis)","tn":"Frozen shoulder (adhesieve capsulitis) – tweede protocol","c":3,"en":"Strong topical DMSO over a frozen shoulder, aimed at stiffness and adhesions.","nl":"Sterk DMSO op de schouder bij een frozen shoulder, gericht op stijfheid en verklevingen.","d":["Apply 70% DMSO in distilled water over the entire shoulder area in a wide circumference twice daily.","Immediately follow with 10–15 sprays of topical magnesium oil over the same area (magnesium absorbs faster after DMSO opens the skin barrier).","Take buffered vitamin C 3,000mg 2–3 times daily to support tissue repair and collagen formation.","Apply natural progesterone cream (100mg from wild yam) twice daily to improve cell-to-cell communication and accelerate healing.","Apply hexane-free castor oil packs over the shoulder for 20 minutes daily to assist mobility and detoxify the joint cavity.","Continue for a full month minimum — tendons and ligaments have low water content and absorb DMSO more slowly than muscle."],"fr":"Twice daily (DMSO + magnesium); once daily (castor oil pack)"},{"t":"Gout","tn":"Jicht","c":3,"en":"Topical use on acutely inflamed gout joints such as the big toe, ankle and knee.","nl":"Aanbrengen op acuut ontstoken jichtgewrichten zoals grote teen, enkel en knie.","d":["During an acute gout attack: apply 50–70% DMSO directly to the inflamed joint using a spray or cotton pad.","For big toe gout: paint DMSO onto the entire toe and metatarsal head area.","Optionally wrap with gauze, then rubber sheeting, then a warm moist compress for 30–60 minutes to amplify the anti-inflammatory effect.","After 12 hours of intensive treatment (maximum 3 sessions), wash the foot and apply aloe vera.","Elevate the affected limb to reduce swelling.","Reapply every 4–6 hours during the acute attack."],"fr":"Every 4–6 hours during acute gout attack; once daily for sub-acute management"},{"t":"Hammertoes","tn":"Hamertenen","c":3,"en":"Applied to hammertoes to relieve pain from the bent, corn-prone toe.","nl":"Op hamertenen om pijn van de kromme, likdoorngevoelige teen te verlichten.","d":["Cleanse the affected toe and surrounding area thoroughly.","Paint 70% DMSO directly onto the hammertoe deformity — particularly over the raised, contracted area.","Cover with a light impervious plastic dressing to enhance contact.","Leave for several hours; remove and allow the area to dry completely.","Reapply every 2–3 days as needed for ongoing pain relief.","If a corn has formed on the hammertoe, pare the corn first, then apply DMSO for best penetration."],"fr":"Every 2–3 days for pain management"},{"t":"Hands & Fingers – Roll-On Routine","tn":"Handen & vingers – roller-routine","c":3,"en":"A careful roll-on routine for knuckles and finger joints.","nl":"Nauwkeurige roller-routine voor knokkels en vingergewrichten.","d":["Wash hands with warm water and unscented soap; dry thoroughly.","Let the metal or glass roll-on ball make gentle contact with the skin — do not press, just glide.","Move slowly along the top of each finger from base toward the nail, then follow the sides of the knuckles.","Sweep across the back of the hand, following the tendon lines that rise when fingers are extended.","Apply a few long, gentle passes along the thumb webbing.","Allow to air-dry naturally, hands resting open and relaxed. Avoid clasping or touching fabrics until fully dry.","Optionally apply a neutral moisturiser after drying if the hands appreciate extra softness."],"fr":"Daily or as needed — especially after repetitive fine-motor work"},{"t":"Heel Spurs (Calcaneal Spur)","tn":"Hielspoor (calcaneusspoor)","c":3,"en":"Topical use plus an occlusive wrap on the heel for inflamed heel spurs.","nl":"Aanbrengen op de hiel met een afsluitend verband bij een ontstoken hielspoor.","d":["Cleanse the heel and back of the foot thoroughly.","Paint 70–80% DMSO directly onto the heel over the spur site (typically the centre of the heel pad or rear of the heel).","Apply DMSO under an impervious plastic wrap, held in place with padding — leave for 3–4 hours.","For deeper penetration: use DMSO as the coupling medium with ultrasound treatment, directing the transducer over the spur site.","Remove wrap, wash heel, and apply aloe vera or a soothing moisturiser.","Repeat once or twice daily during painful periods."],"fr":"Once or twice daily during acute pain"},{"t":"Hip osteoarthritis","tn":"Heupartrose","c":3,"en":"Pain support for hip osteoarthritis alongside walking and strength training.","nl":"Pijnondersteuning bij heupartrose naast loop- en krachttraining.","d":["50–70% to lateral hip once daily–twice daily (morning and evening); abductor training."],"fr":"Twice daily"},{"t":"IT band syndrome","tn":"IT-bandsyndroom (lopersknie)","c":3,"en":"Local application for IT band syndrome, together with hip strengthening.","nl":"Plaatselijk aanbrengen bij het ITB-syndroom (lopersknie), samen met heupversterking.","d":["40–60% along ITB once daily; abductor work."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Knee osteoarthritis","tn":"Knieartrose","c":3,"en":"Relief of pain and stiffness in knee osteoarthritis, combined with exercise.","nl":"Verlichting van pijn en stijfheid bij knieartrose, gecombineerd met beweging.","d":["50–70% to knee 2–3×/day; strength & mobility."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Knees – Daily Relief Routine","tn":"Knieën – dagelijkse verlichting","c":3,"en":"An end-of-day knee routine built on precise, consistent application.","nl":"Dagelijkse avondroutine voor de knieën, gericht op nauwkeurig en regelmatig aanbrengen.","d":["Wash the knee area thoroughly with warm water and an unscented soap; dry completely.","Apply a thin, even layer of your DMSO blend — roll-on for precision around the joint line; spray for fast coverage; fingertip for slow, intentional application.","Bend and extend the knee softly while seated — no force, just enough movement to help the blend settle around the patella and side ligaments.","Allow to air-dry completely before clothing touches the area.","Optionally follow with a neutral moisturiser or aloe gel once dry.","Place a warm cloth over the knee after drying for additional comfort after a demanding day."],"fr":"Daily — ideally at the end of the day"},{"t":"Knees – Post-Activity Care","tn":"Knieën – verzorging na inspanning","c":3,"en":"Knee care right after exercise, while the tissues are still warm.","nl":"Kniezorg direct na het sporten, terwijl het weefsel nog warm is.","d":["Give the knee 1–2 quiet minutes after activity before applying — let muscle tension begin to fade naturally.","Apply your DMSO blend in broad, sweeping strokes around the whole knee: the front, sides, and just above and below the kneecap.","Use a spray or roll-on — sprays cover quickly without touching sensitive regions; roll-ons glide easily over warm skin.","Let the product dry while the knee remains supported and still — avoid bending or flexing during drying.","Optionally finish with a cool damp cloth placed lightly over the area after drying, especially after long weight-bearing periods."],"fr":"After each activity session"},{"t":"Knees – Sleep-Support Nighttime Routine","tn":"Knieën – nachtroutine voor betere slaap","c":3,"en":"A night-time routine for knee discomfort that disturbs sleep, including the surrounding calf muscles.","nl":"Avondroutine voor kniepijn die de slaap verstoort, inclusief de omliggende kuitspieren.","d":["About 1 hour before bed, apply a thin layer of DMSO blend to the knees and surrounding muscles.","For a warm, relaxing sensation: use a magnesium + DMSO blend.","For sensitive skin or a softer nighttime feel: use an aloe + DMSO blend.","Allow to absorb, then move gently — ankle circles, slow knee bends — to signal the body to soften.","After a few minutes allow the area to settle fully before sleep."],"fr":"Nightly — approximately 1 hour before bed"},{"t":"Lateral epicondylitis (tennis elbow)","tn":"Tenniselleboog (epicondylitis lateralis)","c":3,"en":"Support for tennis elbow, together with eccentric strengthening.","nl":"Ondersteuning bij tenniselleboog, samen met excentrische krachtoefeningen.","d":["50–70% to lateral elbow once daily–twice daily (morning and evening) × 2–3 weeks."],"fr":"Twice daily"},{"t":"Low back pain (muscular)","tn":"Lage rugpijn (spierpijn)","c":3,"en":"A comfort add-on for muscular low back pain alongside mobility work.","nl":"Verlichtende aanvulling bij spierpijn in de onderrug, naast bewegingsoefeningen.","d":["40–70% to paraspinals once daily; core/hip work."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Lower Back – Targeted Application Protocol","tn":"Onderrug – gerichte toepassing","c":3,"en":"A structured lumbar routine using horizontal strokes across the lower back.","nl":"Gestructureerde routine voor de onderrug met horizontale strijkbewegingen.","d":["Find a posture that frees the lower back — stand with feet apart, lean onto a counter, or rest one foot on a low stool.","Cleanse the skin over the lower back with warm water or a damp cloth.","Apply DMSO blend using slow, horizontal strokes following the natural width of the lumbar region — spray for broad coverage; roll-on to trace the spine or outer lumbar edges.","If applying with hands, use smooth sweeping arcs from one side of the waist toward the other — no inward pressing.","Allow to air-dry fully before waistbands, belts, or elastic touches the area.","Once dry, optionally place a warm compress over the lumbar region for 5–10 minutes; use a cool compress after prolonged standing."],"fr":"Once or twice daily, or as needed"},{"t":"Lower Body vs Upper Body – Tailored DMSO Application Routines","tn":"Onder- en bovenlichaam – DMSO-routines op maat","c":3,"en":"Explains how to adapt technique for the lower versus the upper body.","nl":"Legt uit hoe je de techniek aanpast voor onderlichaam versus bovenlichaam.","d":["LOWER BODY APPROACH — Length & Grounding: Apply DMSO using broad, steady strokes that follow the full length of the muscles — thighs, calves, and hips benefit from long, continuous motions that acknowledge their size and the work they do daily.","LOWER BODY — Allow the legs to rest openly after application, releasing the dense, accumulated heaviness that settles after long hours of movement or standing.","UPPER BODY APPROACH — Precision & Subtlety: Use shorter, more deliberate motions — the roll-on traces places where strain naturally gathers: the outer edge of the shoulder, the small groove beside the neck, or the upper ridge of the traps where posture has been pulling for hours.","UPPER BODY — Move with intention rather than coverage. Follow the natural contours of intricate upper-body muscles rather than broad sweeping strokes.","AS PRODUCT SETTLES: Lower body — muscles often feel as though sinking deeper into rest, released from carried weight. Upper body — tends to soften gradually, as if the shoulders are remembering they no longer need to stay lifted.","Allow everything to dry fully before clothing meets the skin."],"fr":"Adapt your technique every time you apply DMSO — the area dictates the approach"},{"t":"Medial epicondylitis (golfer’s elbow)","tn":"Golferselleboog (epicondylitis medialis)","c":3,"en":"Focused application on the inner elbow for golfer's elbow.","nl":"Gerichte toepassing aan de binnenkant van de elleboog bij golferselleboog.","d":["50–70% to medial elbow once daily–twice daily (morning and evening) × 2–3 weeks."],"fr":"Twice daily"},{"t":"Metatarsalgia (Morton's Toe)","tn":"Metatarsalgie (voorvoetpijn, mortonteen)","c":3,"en":"DMSO as a carrier for local anaesthetic injections in forefoot pain; a medical procedure.","nl":"DMSO als drager bij verdovingsinjecties tegen pijn in de voorvoet; een medische ingreep.","d":["For acute severe pain (clinical procedure): local anaesthetic mixed with DMSO injected slowly into the inflamed nerve site in the foot. DMSO carries the anaesthetic deeper for more complete and lasting relief.","For conservative management: apply 50–70% DMSO topically to the ball of the foot and between the third and fourth metatarsal heads using a roll-on.","Combine with a metatarsal pad placed in the shoe to spread the metatarsal heads and reduce nerve compression.","Apply DMSO once daily — allow to fully absorb before putting on footwear."],"fr":"Once daily for topical use; injection protocol per podiatrist/physician"},{"t":"Mid & Upper Back – DMSO Routine","tn":"Midden- & bovenrug – DMSO-routine","c":3,"en":"A routine for the mid and upper back, the area that holds postural and stress tension.","nl":"Routine voor midden- en bovenrug, waar houdings- en stressspanning zich ophoopt.","d":["Position thoughtfully: stand against a mirror, or sit on the edge of a bed with arms falling forward to open the space between shoulder blades.","Cleanse the upper and mid-back — remove sweat, fabric softener residues, and hair product traces.","Use a spray: move in smooth diagonal lines from shoulder toward the spine, or from spine outward toward the ribcage.","If using a roll-on: trace around the shoulder blades, glide along the inner edge of the scapula, then follow the line toward the top of the shoulders.","Allow to air-dry fully before straps, collars, or fabric seams contact the area.","Optionally place a warm cloth across the shoulder blades after drying; or a cool compress after long desk hours."],"fr":"As needed — daily for chronic tension; after demanding postural periods"},{"t":"Muscle Recovery – Post-Exercise","tn":"Spierherstel – na het sporten","c":3,"en":"A post-workout routine for muscle recovery, applied when the skin is warm and receptive.","nl":"Routine na de training voor spierherstel, aangebracht als de huid nog warm is.","d":["Give the body a few minutes to settle after exercise — allow breathing to return to a gentle rhythm.","Cleanse the target area with warm water and unscented soap to remove sweat salts and fabric fibres.","Apply a thin, even layer of DMSO blend — roll-on for calves or forearms; spray for thighs, back, or chest; hands for intuitive slow coverage.","Allow to air-dry fully before clothing contacts the skin.","Optionally layer aloe vera gel or a neutral moisturiser over the dried area.","Follow with a warm cloth if the muscles feel engaged; a cool cloth if they feel overcharged from intense effort."],"fr":"After each workout or physical activity session"},{"t":"Muscle Repair & Wasting – DMSO + L-Glutamine + MSM Protocol","tn":"Spierherstel & spierafbraak – DMSO + L-glutamine + MSM","c":3,"en":"Combines DMSO with L-glutamine and MSM for muscle injury and muscle wasting.","nl":"DMSO samen met L-glutamine en MSM bij spierletsel en spierafbraak.","d":["Apply 1 tablespoon of 50–70% DMSO solution over the injured or wasting muscles twice daily.","Take 4.5–5g of L-glutamine amino acid daily (the primary amino acid for muscle repair).","Take ½ teaspoon of MSM sulfur crystals twice daily to support collagen and muscle tissue integrity.","HYDROTHERAPY: Apply a hot compress for 3 minutes followed by a cold compress for 30 seconds. Repeat 5 times, ending on cold. This mobilises lymphatic clearance of cellular waste from the muscles.","Once past the acute injury phase, begin gentle exercise guided by a physiotherapist, chiropractor, or osteopathic doctor to prevent muscle imbalances.","Weekly professional massage or acupuncture helps maintain circulation and muscular balance."],"fr":"Twice daily (DMSO); hydrotherapy as needed"},{"t":"Muscle Strains & Tension Areas","tn":"Spierverrekkingen & gespannen plekken","c":3,"en":"A flexible routine for strain-prone spots like neck, shoulders, lower back and hamstrings.","nl":"Flexibele routine voor blessuregevoelige plekken als nek, schouders, onderrug en hamstrings.","d":["Bring the body into a relaxed posture before applying — let shoulders fall, soften the jaw, release the abdomen.","Cleanse the skin lightly if the area has been under clothing or exposed to sweat or lotions.","Apply a thin, measured layer of DMSO blend: roll-on for lines across the neck or shoulder ridge; spray for the lumbar region or upper back; hands using long strokes for large muscles.","Allow the blend to sit lightly on the skin — do not rub or work it in.","Keep the body still and avoid compressing the area with clothing or posture while it dries.","Once dry, optionally apply a warming cloth for deep or stubborn tension, or a cool cloth for overworked areas."],"fr":"As needed at the first signal of tension"},{"t":"Neck – Blended DMSO Compress","tn":"Nek – DMSO-kompres met mengsel","c":3,"en":"A calm, meditative neck compress using a cloth moistened with a DMSO blend.","nl":"Rustgevend nekkompres met een doek bevochtigd met een DMSO-mengsel.","d":["Prepare a soft, clean, white or undyed cotton cloth — soak lightly in your DMSO blend diluted with water; damp, not dripping.","Cleanse the neck with warm water and unscented cleanser — removing hair product, perfume, sweat, or collar residues.","Drape the cloth gently along the sides or back of the neck, following the contours where tightness gathers.","Leave for 5–15 minutes, or until the cloth begins to lose its warmth or coolness.","Keep the head supported and avoid sudden movements during the compress.","Remove the cloth and allow the skin to air-dry completely before dressing.","Optionally apply a thin layer of aloe or neutral moisturiser afterward."],"fr":"As needed — particularly for end-of-day neck tension"},{"t":"Neck – Digital Strain Protocol","tn":"Nek – klachten door schermgebruik","c":3,"en":"Aimed at \"tech neck\", the tightness at the skull base from screen use.","nl":"Gericht op de 'beeldschermnek': spanning aan de schedelbasis door veel schermgebruik.","d":["Step away from the screen; lift the head slowly and let the gaze return to the horizon.","Cleanse the neck quickly with a damp cloth if perfume, hair products, or sunscreen are present.","Apply a light amount of DMSO blend along the sides of the neck — begin just below the ears and glide downward along the long vertical muscles.","Use a roll-on for precise lines; use a spray at short distance to keep the product targeted and away from hair.","Gently float the chin upward a few centimetres to open the front of the neck — no stretching, just widening.","Let the product air-dry while keeping shoulders relaxed and breath easy.","Once dry, reset posture: shoulder blades soften downward, chin to neutral, crown of head lifting gently."],"fr":"As needed — mid-morning, mid-afternoon, or between work sessions"},{"t":"Osteoarthritis – DMSO + MSM + Vitamins D & K2 Protocol","tn":"Artrose – DMSO + MSM + vitamine D & K2","c":3,"en":"An osteoarthritis plan combining skin DMSO with oral MSM and vitamins D and K2.","nl":"Artroseplan met DMSO op de huid plus MSM en vitamine D en K2 via de mond.","d":["TOPICAL DMSO: Apply 70% DMSO in distilled water or aloe vera gel over all affected joints in a wide circumference, 2–3 times daily.","ORAL MSM: Take ½ teaspoon (approx. 2g) of MSM sulfur crystals twice daily. Work up to 1 tsp twice daily for severe cases. Use crystals, not capsules — they release more slowly and are more effective.","VITAMINS D & K2: Take 5,000 IU vitamin D3 (or D2 for vegans) with 400–600 IU vitamin K2 at dinner daily. K2 directs calcium into bones rather than soft tissue.","TOPICAL MAGNESIUM: Apply 10–15 sprays of magnesium oil over affected joints immediately after DMSO, twice daily.","CASTOR OIL WARM PACKS: Apply warm castor oil packs over inflamed joints for 20 minutes before topical DMSO for best effect.","For severe cases or large joints (hip, knee, shoulder): consider DMSO injections rather than topical — consult a physician."],"fr":"DMSO 2–3 times daily; MSM twice daily; vitamins daily"},{"t":"Osteomyelitis (Bone Infection) – DMSO + Antibiotic","tn":"Osteomyelitis (botinfectie) – DMSO + antibiotica","c":3,"en":"Intravenous DMSO with antibiotics for bone infection; strictly a hospital treatment.","nl":"DMSO via een infuus samen met antibiotica bij botinfectie; puur een ziekenhuisbehandeling.","d":["DMSO for osteomyelitis is administered intravenously in combination with appropriate antibiotics — hospital/medical setting only.","Topical DMSO (70%) applied to the skin overlying the infected bone area twice daily can provide supportive benefit alongside IV treatment.","Oral DMSO (1 teaspoon in juice 2–3 times daily) may be used as an adjunct in less severe cases.","Continue antibiotic treatment as prescribed; DMSO is added to, not substituted for, the antibiotic regimen.","Monitor with imaging and blood markers — resolution of infection should be confirmed before stopping treatment."],"fr":"Daily IV (hospital); twice daily topical adjunct"},{"t":"Patellar tendinopathy","tn":"Springersknie (patellapeesklachten)","c":3,"en":"Support for jumper's knee alongside isometric and eccentric training.","nl":"Ondersteuning bij springersknie naast isometrische en excentrische training.","d":["40–70% to patellar tendon once daily; loading plan."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Phantom Limb Pain","tn":"Fantoompijn","c":3,"en":"A lotion with DMSO, capsicum and aloe on the amputation site for phantom pain.","nl":"Lotion met DMSO, capsicum en aloë op de amputatieplek tegen fantoompijn.","d":["Prepare or obtain a DMSO lotion containing: 70–90% DMSO + capsicum pepper extract + aloe vera juice.","Apply the lotion twice daily to the amputation stump and the immediate surrounding area.","Apply whether or not pain is present — continue even on pain-free days.","Continue for at least 3 months. In the documented case, the phantom pain did not return after 3 months of treatment.","Oral DMSO (1 teaspoon in cranberry juice daily) may enhance the systemic nerve-modulating effect."],"fr":"Twice daily (topical); once daily (oral)"},{"t":"Plantar fasciitis","tn":"Fasciitis plantaris (ontstoken voetzool)","c":3,"en":"An add-on for the morning heel pain and stiffness of plantar fasciitis.","nl":"Aanvulling bij de ochtendpijn en stijfheid van fasciitis plantaris.","d":["40–70% to heel/arch once daily; stretches."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Post-Surgical Pain Management","tn":"Pijnbestrijding na een operatie","c":3,"en":"Topical DMSO around surgical wounds for pain after an operation; involves medical oversight.","nl":"DMSO rond operatiewonden tegen pijn na een ingreep; vraagt medische afstemming.","d":["Apply 50–70% DMSO directly to the closed surgical incision and surrounding area every 6 hours.","Application should begin as soon as the surgical site can be accessed post-operatively (skin must be intact and wound closed).","Allow to dry fully before covering with dressings.","Continue for the duration of the post-operative pain period — typically 3–7 days.","Monitor the surgical site for any unusual reaction — reduce concentration if skin irritation develops."],"fr":"Every 6 hours post-operatively"},{"t":"Shin splints (MTSS)","tn":"Scheenbeenvliesontsteking (MTSS)","c":3,"en":"Reduced training load plus local application for shin splints.","nl":"Minder belasting plus plaatselijk aanbrengen bij scheenbeenvliesontsteking.","d":["40–70% along medial tibial border once daily × 2–3 weeks."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Shoulder impingement / rotator cuff","tn":"Schouderimpingement / rotator cuff","c":3,"en":"Topical use over the shoulder during rehab for impingement or rotator cuff problems.","nl":"Op de schouder tijdens revalidatie bij inklemming of rotatorcuffklachten.","d":["40–60% once daily; RC and scapular exercises."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Shoulder Tendons – Focused DMSO Care","tn":"Schouderpezen – gerichte DMSO-verzorging","c":3,"en":"A shoulder-tendon routine using curved strokes that follow the joint.","nl":"Schouderpeesroutine met gebogen strijkbewegingen die het gewricht volgen.","d":["Set the arm in a comfortable, supported position — resting at the side or on a cushion.","Clean the skin over the front and side of the shoulder — remove deodorant and fabric contact residue.","Apply a thin layer of blend using smooth, curved motions that follow the shape of the joint.","Use a roll-on to trace natural arcs where tension gathers; use a controlled spray for broader coverage.","Wait until the skin feels dry before moving the arm or allowing clothing to contact the area.","Once dry, add a warm or cool cloth depending on what feels most pleasant."],"fr":"As needed — daily for ongoing shoulder restriction or overuse"},{"t":"Shoulders – Heat & Cold Pairing","tn":"Schouders – combinatie van warmte & kou","c":3,"en":"Pairs shoulder application with warm and cold cloths to enhance the effect.","nl":"Combineert aanbrengen op de schouder met warme en koude doeken voor meer effect.","d":["Apply your DMSO blend to the shoulder and allow it to dry completely.","For a shoulder that feels tight, contracted, or stiff from posture: drape a warm cloth or lightly heated pack over the upper trap and deltoid for 5–10 minutes.","For a shoulder that feels flushed, overheated, or overworked from activity: place a cool cloth over the dried area instead.","If the signal isn't obvious, skip temperature pairing — the DMSO blend can stand on its own.","Remove after 5–10 minutes and allow the area to settle naturally."],"fr":"After each DMSO shoulder application, as needed"},{"t":"Shoulders – Targeted Application","tn":"Schouders – gerichte toepassing","c":3,"en":"Precise application over the upper trapezius and deltoid region.","nl":"Precies aanbrengen op de bovenste monnikskapspier en de deltaspier.","d":["Cleanse the shoulder skin — removing deodorant, hair product, sweat, and lotion residues.","Use a roll-on for precision: glide along the upper trapezius, trace the deltoid midline, sweep across the back shoulder line, and follow the groove between the shoulder and neck.","Use a spray for broader deltoid coverage — hold close enough for a concentrated, even layer.","Apply with light pressure only — DMSO does not need to be worked in.","Allow the area to air-dry with the arm relaxed: resting at the side, draped over a pillow, or supported by a chair.","Optionally finish with a thin layer of aloe or neutral moisturiser once dry."],"fr":"As needed — daily for chronic tension; after demanding periods"},{"t":"Tendinitis – High-Concentration DMSO Protocol (80–90%)","tn":"Peesontsteking – hooggeconcentreerde DMSO (80–90%)","c":3,"en":"Very strong DMSO over inflamed tendons in shoulder, elbow, wrist or knee; skin tolerance is a concern.","nl":"Zeer sterk DMSO op ontstoken pezen in schouder, elleboog, pols of knie; let op huidverdraagzaamheid.","d":["CASTOR OIL PREPARATION: Apply a hexane-free castor oil pack with a hot water bottle over the tendon for 20 minutes first, to increase local blood flow.","Wash off the castor oil with baking soda solution (1 tsp baking soda in ½ cup water). Ensure skin is completely clean.","Apply 80% DMSO (or 90% for stubborn cases) in a wide circumference around the tendon area.","Leave treated area open to air for 15–20 minutes.","FREQUENCY: Initially every 4–6 hours for the first few days, then 2–3 times daily. The rate can be adjusted based on individual response.","Between applications, moisturise the skin with raw olive oil to prevent dryness from repeated high-concentration applications.","90% DMSO in studies: applied every 4 hours, duration of 3 weeks. All subjects reported fair, good, or excellent results."],"fr":"Every 4–6 hours initially; 2–3 times daily for ongoing treatment"},{"t":"Tendonitis / bursitis (shoulder/elbow/hip)","tn":"Peesontsteking / slijmbeursontsteking (schouder/elleboog/heup)","c":3,"en":"Local applications to ease tendon or bursa pain at common sites like shoulder, elbow and hip.","nl":"Plaatselijk aanbrengen bij pees- of slijmbeurspijn in schouder, elleboog en heup.","d":["50–70% a very light layer (just enough to make the skin shiny, not wet) 1–2×/day for 1–2 weeks."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Trigger finger (tenosynovitis)","tn":"Triggervinger (tendovaginitis)","c":3,"en":"Focused application over the affected finger tendon in trigger finger.","nl":"Gericht aanbrengen op de aangedane vingerpees bij een triggervinger.","d":["40–70% to palmar MCP crease once daily × 2–3 weeks."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Anxiety & Obsessive-Compulsive Disorder – DMSO Adjunct","tn":"Angst & dwangstoornis – DMSO als aanvulling","c":4,"en":"Describes DMSO injections as a historical add-on for severe anxiety and OCD; strictly a medical treatment.","nl":"Beschrijft DMSO-injecties als historische aanvulling bij ernstige angst en dwangstoornis; puur medische behandeling.","d":["Intramuscular DMSO injections at 50% concentration, 1–2 times daily — physician administered.","Topical DMSO applied to the back of the neck and upper shoulders may provide a calming effect even without injection.","Oral DMSO (1 teaspoon in juice once or twice daily) can be used as a milder adjunct for anxiety management.","DMSO’s tranquilising properties mean even skin application has been observed to calm agitation — it can be applied topically as a first step."],"fr":"Daily (injection or oral/topical adjunct)"},{"t":"Concussion / head injury (adjunct)","tn":"Hersenschudding / hoofdletsel (aanvullend)","c":4,"en":"Cites older protocols on membrane protection after concussion or head injury; supervision required.","nl":"Verwijst naar oudere protocollen over celbescherming na hersenschudding of hoofdletsel; toezicht vereist."},{"t":"Diabetes – Circulation & Amputation Prevention","tn":"Diabetes – doorbloeding & voorkomen van amputatie","c":4,"en":"Topical and oral DMSO for poor circulation and nerve damage in diabetes, framed as helping prevent amputation.","nl":"DMSO via huid en mond bij slechte doorbloeding en zenuwschade door diabetes, gepresenteerd als hulp om amputatie te voorkomen.","d":["Apply DMSO topically at 50–70% to both feet and legs twice daily — cover the entire foot including all toes.","Simultaneously take 1 teaspoon of DMSO in juice every evening after dinner.","Continue strictly following a diabetic diet and prescribed insulin regimen — do not reduce insulin without physician approval.","Follow any exercise programme prescribed by a doctor alongside DMSO treatment.","Monitor circulation, sensation in feet, and toe colour regularly — improvement in sensation should occur within a few weeks."],"fr":"Twice daily topical; once daily oral"},{"t":"Down Syndrome – DMSO + Amino Acid Therapy","tn":"Downsyndroom – DMSO + aminozuurtherapie","c":4,"en":"Reports a Chilean study pairing DMSO with amino acid injections in Down syndrome; experimental medical use.","nl":"Noemt een Chileens onderzoek met DMSO en aminozuurinjecties bij downsyndroom; experimenteel en medisch.","d":["Injection vials: 5cc of 5% DMSO + 5mg GABA + 10mg GABOB + 10mg acetyl glutamine, administered intramuscularly.","CHILDREN UNDER 3.5 YEARS: dose adjusted by body weight (½ cc for <8kg, 1cc for 8–11kg, 2cc for >11kg). Injections every other day for 90 days, then 1 month break with amino acid capsules only. Minimum 3 cycles.","CHILDREN OVER 3.5 YEARS: full 5cc ampule per injection, daily for 20 days, then 20 days off with amino acid capsules. 5 series of 20 injections total.","SIMPLER HOME PROTOCOL: 1 teaspoon of DMSO in milk or juice daily (as used by Billy King) — a low-cost, accessible starting point.","All protocols should be overseen by a paediatrician or developmental specialist."],"fr":"Daily or every other day depending on protocol; oral daily"},{"t":"Hemorrhagic & Embolic Stroke (Emergency Adjunct)","tn":"Hersenbloeding & herseninfarct (aanvulling bij spoed)","c":4,"en":"Intravenous DMSO as an emergency add-on for both bleeding and clot-related stroke; hospital only.","nl":"DMSO via infuus als noodaanvulling bij zowel hersenbloeding als herseninfarct; alleen in het ziekenhuis.","d":["DMSO for stroke is an intravenous emergency protocol — strictly hospital/emergency room administration.","Dose: 40% DMSO solution, 1 gram per kilogram body weight, given intravenously as rapidly as possible after stroke onset.","Best effect: within 90 minutes of stroke onset. Some benefit reported up to 4–6 hours post-event.","DMSO reduces intracranial pressure within 3–5 minutes of IV administration — faster than barbiturates or mannitol.","This is emergency medicine and must be administered by qualified medical personnel in a clinical setting."],"fr":"Single emergency IV administration; follow-up doses per neurosurgeon direction"},{"t":"Intracranial Hypertension (Head Injury Adjunct)","tn":"Verhoogde hersendruk (aanvulling bij hoofdletsel)","c":4,"en":"Intravenous DMSO to lower dangerous brain pressure after head injury, in intensive care.","nl":"DMSO via infuus om gevaarlijk hoge hersendruk na hoofdletsel te verlagen, op de intensive care.","d":["10% or 20% DMSO solution administered intravenously in a hospital setting, titrated against the intracranial pressure monitor.","A bolus (push) injection of 10% DMSO has been used for rapid ICP reduction.","A 20% solution titrated slowly against ICP readings provides more sustained control.","Electrolytes and fluid balance must be carefully monitored during DMSO ICP treatment.","Strictly a hospital neurological/neurosurgical procedure."],"fr":"Single or repeated IV administrations under neurosurgeon monitoring"},{"t":"Manic Depression & Alcoholic Psychosis – DMSO Adjunct","tn":"Manisch-depressieve stoornis & alcoholpsychose – DMSO als aanvulling","c":4,"en":"Historical intramuscular DMSO as an add-on for mania and alcohol-related psychosis.","nl":"Historische spierinjecties met DMSO als aanvulling bij manie en alcoholpsychose.","d":["Begin DMSO treatment with all previous psychiatric medications withdrawn for at least 1 week (under psychiatrist supervision).","Administer 5ml intramuscular injections of 80% DMSO, 2–3 times daily during the acute manic or psychotic phase.","As agitation reduces, shift to 50% DMSO solution.","For alcoholic psychosis with delirium tremens: start DMSO immediately — restlessness and hallucinations decrease within first few days.","Combine with appropriate medical detoxification and addiction support."],"fr":"2–3 times daily during acute phase"},{"t":"Migraine/neck tension (adjunct)","tn":"Migraine / nekspanning (aanvullend)","c":4,"en":"Some report relief from applying around the neck for migraine and neck tension.","nl":"Sommigen melden verlichting door rond de nek aan te brengen bij migraine en nekspanning.","d":["20–40% to suboccipital/neck skin; avoid mucosa."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Multiple Sclerosis (Adjunct)","tn":"Multiple sclerose (aanvullend)","c":4,"en":"Presents DMSO as an add-on in MS, citing favourable immune effects.","nl":"DMSO als aanvulling bij MS, met verwijzing naar gunstige effecten op het afweersysteem.","d":["Topical DMSO applied to areas of numbness, weakness, or spasticity: 50–70% concentration, applied 1–2 times daily.","For limb spasticity or weakness: apply along the affected limb from proximal to distal, allow to fully absorb.","For bladder involvement (neurogenic bladder in MS): intravesical DMSO instillation may be considered — medical procedure.","Oral DMSO has been studied for systemic MS effects — under medical supervision only.","Combine with gentle physiotherapy and range-of-motion exercises after topical application."],"fr":"Once or twice daily for topical use; systemic protocols under medical direction"},{"t":"Myasthenia Gravis (Adjunct)","tn":"Myasthenia gravis (aanvullend)","c":4,"en":"Claims DMSO lowered the abnormal antibodies in myasthenia gravis in research; medical context.","nl":"Stelt dat DMSO in onderzoek de afwijkende antistoffen bij myasthenie verlaagde; medische context.","d":["DMSO for myasthenia gravis is at the research stage — there is no established topical or oral protocol proven in human clinical trials.","Animal studies: DMSO reduced abnormal acetylcholine-receptor antibodies more effectively than the immunosuppressive drug frentizole it was carrying.","Topical DMSO applied to affected muscle groups (neck, shoulders, eyes) may provide supportive symptomatic relief.","Any systemic DMSO use for myasthenia gravis must be discussed with a neurologist and undertaken under medical supervision."],"fr":"Supportive topical use as needed; systemic protocols under neurologist direction"},{"t":"Peripheral neuropathy (adjunct)","tn":"Perifere neuropathie (aanvullend)","c":4,"en":"Support for burning and tingling in nerve damage, together with nutritional support.","nl":"Ondersteuning bij branderige en tintelende zenuwpijn, samen met voedingsstoffen.","d":["30–50% to affected dermatomes once daily; B‑vitamins/ALA."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Post‑herpetic neuralgia","tn":"Postherpetische neuralgie (zenuwpijn na gordelroos)","c":4,"en":"Topical use for nerve pain lingering after shingles.","nl":"Op de huid bij zenuwpijn die na gordelroos blijft hangen.","d":["40–70% a very light layer (just enough to make the skin shiny, not wet) 1–2×/day; titrate."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Restless Leg Syndrome – DMSO + Magnesium Evening Protocol","tn":"Rustelozebenensyndroom – DMSO + magnesium in de avond","c":4,"en":"Evening application to legs and feet, combined with magnesium, for restless legs.","nl":"Avondlijk insmeren van benen en voeten, gecombineerd met magnesium, bij rusteloze benen.","d":["Before bed: wash legs and feet thoroughly.","Apply 70% DMSO to clean legs and feet — cover from ankle to knee. Allow to dry for 10–15 minutes.","Apply magnesium oil liberally over the same area and allow to dry before getting into bed.","Take B vitamins in the morning after breakfast (not in the evening — they provide energy and may disrupt sleep).","Take 50mg zinc picolinate once daily with food (not on an empty stomach — may cause nausea).","Ensure adequate iron in diet; take vitamin C alongside iron supplements to improve absorption.","Avoid caffeine, alcohol, and tobacco in the evening as these worsen RLS."],"fr":"Nightly before bed"},{"t":"Schizophrenia (Acute) – DMSO Injection Protocol","tn":"Schizofrenie (acuut) – DMSO-injectie","c":4,"en":"Reports a Peruvian study of intramuscular DMSO in acute schizophrenia; purely clinical.","nl":"Noemt Peruaans onderzoek met spierinjecties DMSO bij acute schizofrenie; uitsluitend klinisch.","d":["Discontinue all previous psychiatric medications for at least 1 week before starting DMSO (under psychiatrist supervision).","Begin with 5ml intramuscular injections of 80% DMSO, 2–3 times daily for acutely disturbed patients; up to 5 injections daily for most severely agitated patients.","As symptoms improve, reduce to 50% DMSO concentration.","Combine with B-12 injections and GH3 for enhanced effect in chronic paranoid cases.","For chronic patients: continue treatment; relapsed patients respond to re-treatment with the same improvement as initial treatment."],"fr":"2–5 injections daily for acute phase; reducing as patient stabilises"},{"t":"Sciatic nerve irritation (adjunct)","tn":"Geïrriteerde heupzenuw (aanvullend)","c":4,"en":"Topical use along the buttock and back of the thigh for sciatic irritation, with mobility work.","nl":"Langs bil en achterkant dijbeen bij geïrriteerde heupzenuw, samen met bewegen.","d":["30–50% along course once daily; nerve‑glide work."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Senile Dementia & Alzheimer's – DMSO Adjunct","tn":"Ouderdomsdementie & alzheimer – DMSO als aanvulling","c":4,"en":"Historical DMSO therapies with amino acids or circulation drugs for dementia and Alzheimer's.","nl":"Historische DMSO-therapieën met aminozuren of vaatmiddelen bij dementie en alzheimer.","d":["DMSO-amino acid therapy (Merinex): oral capsules and intramuscular injections alternated daily for a cycle of 20 injections, then oral maintenance.","DMSO combined with vasoactive substances (Ipran): intramuscular injection daily for 20 injections, then every other day for 30 more injections, alongside oral capsules twice daily.","Both therapies may be combined and given simultaneously for faster response.","These are medical protocols requiring physician direction. They use DMSO-based injectable compounds not currently approved by the FDA.","Topical DMSO applied to the scalp and back of the neck is a supportive measure that may improve local circulation."],"fr":"Medical protocol: daily injections for several weeks, then tapering; topical supportive use daily"},{"t":"Spinal Cord Injury – Emergency DMSO Protocol","tn":"Dwarslaesie – DMSO bij spoed","c":4,"en":"Emergency intravenous DMSO soon after a spinal cord injury to limit damage; hospital only.","nl":"Spoedinfuus met DMSO kort na een dwarslaesie om schade te beperken; alleen in het ziekenhuis.","d":["DMSO for spinal cord injury is strictly an intravenous emergency medical protocol.","Dose: 1 gram per kilogram body weight (40% concentration) IV — given as quickly as possible after injury.","Optimal window: within 90 minutes of injury. Some benefit reported up to 6–9 hours post-injury in clinical cases.","Must be administered in an emergency room or trauma centre by qualified medical personnel.","DMSO increases spinal cord blood flow, reduces oedema, protects neurons from enzymatic damage, and restores EEG activity."],"fr":"Single emergency IV dose; follow-up per neurosurgeon direction"},{"t":"Temporal Arteritis (Adjunct)","tn":"Arteriitis temporalis (aanvullend)","c":4,"en":"Topical use on forehead and neck as an add-on for temporal arteritis, alongside medical care.","nl":"Op voorhoofd en nek als aanvulling bij arteriitis temporalis (reuscelarteriitis), naast medische zorg.","d":["Apply 20ml of 50% DMSO twice daily to the entire forehead area and back of the neck.","Pain relief typically occurs within 30 minutes of application.","Continue for one month — in the clinical report, pressure on the temporal artery no longer triggered pain after one month of treatment.","Temporal arteritis requires cortisone therapy as the primary treatment — DMSO is used alongside cortisone, not as a replacement.","Clean the forehead and neck thoroughly before each application to remove any cosmetic, sunscreen, or haircare residues."],"fr":"Twice daily for one month; reduce frequency once relief is established"},{"t":"Trigeminal neuralgia (adjunct)","tn":"Trigeminusneuralgie (aanvullend)","c":4,"en":"Very cautious application around the face for trigeminal nerve pain.","nl":"Zeer voorzichtig rond het gezicht aanbrengen bij aangezichtszenuwpijn.","d":["20–30% to small peri‑facial areas; stop if irritation."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Anal fissure (adjunct)","tn":"Anale fissuur (aanvullend)","c":5,"en":"Weak application around the anus for fissure comfort, keeping it off the tear itself.","nl":"Zwak rond de anus voor verlichting bij een fissuur, maar niet op het scheurtje zelf.","d":["10–20% to perianal skin once daily; stool‑softening; sitz baths."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Cirrhosis of the Liver (Adjunct)","tn":"Levercirrose (aanvullend)","c":5,"en":"Oral DMSO in aloe juice as an add-on for liver cirrhosis, citing one study.","nl":"DMSO in aloëvera-sap via de mond als aanvulling bij levercirrose, op basis van één onderzoek.","d":["Give 1 teaspoon of DMSO in 1 ounce of aloe vera juice twice daily.","Continue for a minimum of 6 months.","Complete alcohol cessation is mandatory — patients who continue drinking will not benefit.","Monitor liver function tests (LFTs) monthly throughout treatment.","Combine with dietary improvements, adequate hydration, and elimination of any other liver-damaging substances."],"fr":"Twice daily"},{"t":"Cryopreservation (cells/tissue)","tn":"Invriezen van cellen/weefsel (cryopreservatie)","c":5,"en":"Explains DMSO's long-standing lab and clinic role in freezing cells and tissue.","nl":"Legt de vaste rol van DMSO uit bij het invriezen van cellen en weefsel in lab en kliniek."},{"t":"Duodenal Ulcers – DMSO Oral Protocol","tn":"Twaalfvingerigedarmzweer – DMSO via de mond","c":5,"en":"Oral DMSO in aloe juice for healing duodenal ulcers and preventing relapse.","nl":"DMSO in aloësap via de mond voor het genezen van een twaalfvingerdarmzweer en het voorkomen van terugval.","d":["ACTIVE ULCER: 1 teaspoon of DMSO in 2 ounces of aloe vera juice three times daily until the ulcer is confirmed healed by endoscopy.","MAINTENANCE (12 months): 1 teaspoon of DMSO in 2 ounces of aloe vera juice every evening.","Reduce alcohol consumption — social drinking is compatible with the protocol but heavy drinking undermines results.","Monitor monthly during the treatment year; patients can track symptom freedom as a primary indicator.","Chlorophyll capsules and breath mints can manage any DMSO breath odour during treatment."],"fr":"Three times daily for active ulcer; once daily for maintenance"},{"t":"Dysmenorrhoea (adjunct)","tn":"Menstruatiepijn (aanvullend)","c":5,"en":"Application to the lower belly on days with menstrual cramps.","nl":"Op de onderbuik aanbrengen op dagen met menstruatiekrampen.","d":["20–40% a very light layer (just enough to make the skin shiny, not wet) during menses; heat supports."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Endometriosis (adjunct)","tn":"Endometriose (aanvullend)","c":5,"en":"Topical comfort on the abdomen for endometriosis pain.","nl":"Verlichting op de buik bij pijn door endometriose.","d":["30–50% to lower abdomen once daily; avoid mucosa."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Gallstones – Dissolution Adjunct","tn":"Galstenen – aanvulling bij oplossen","c":5,"en":"DMSO as a dissolving aid in medical treatment of gallstones.","nl":"DMSO als oplossend hulpmiddel bij de medische behandeling van galstenen.","d":["Gallstone dissolution with DMSO is a medically supervised procedure involving direct infusion into the biliary tract via catheter.","A 70/30 mixture of methyl tert-butyl ether and DMSO has shown near-complete dissolution of cholesterol stones in clinical studies.","For calcium bilirubinate stones: 90% DMSO combined with 5% hexametaphosphate (HMP) instilled via postoperative or PTCD catheter.","Topical DMSO has no direct role in gallstone treatment — this is an adjunct to medical or surgical gallbladder intervention.","Discuss with a hepatobiliary surgeon whether DMSO-enhanced dissolution protocols are appropriate for your case."],"fr":"As per medical protocol — typically a single or short-term infusion course"},{"t":"Gastritis / peptic ulcer (adjunct)","tn":"Maagontsteking / maagzweer (aanvullend)","c":5,"en":"Mentions old dilute oral protocols for gastritis and ulcers, urging a talk about the risks.","nl":"Noemt oude verdunde orale protocollen bij maagontsteking en maagzweer; bespreek eerst de risico's.","d":["≤20%: ½–1 tsp in water after food; short trial only."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Haemorrhoids – DMSO + Witch Hazel Protocol","tn":"Aambeien – DMSO + toverhazelaar","c":5,"en":"Topical DMSO with witch hazel and herbal support for haemorrhoids.","nl":"DMSO op de huid met hamamelis en kruiden bij aambeien.","d":["Apply a combination of witch hazel and strong black or red raspberry leaf tea to a cotton pad. Gently pat over haemorrhoids as an astringent.","Apply a 40% DMSO solution over the haemorrhoids BEFORE the witch hazel/tea — DMSO enhances delivery of the astringent into the tissue.","Drink 1 teaspoon of DMSO in 150ml (5 oz) of water or juice daily to address the internal GI component.","Drink red raspberry leaf tea daily — it supports the gastrointestinal system which is the root cause of haemorrhoids.","Practise intermittent fasting (skipping breakfast or dinner) to rest the digestive organs during the healing period.","Continue for 2 weeks to ensure deeper haemorrhoids fully heal."],"fr":"Daily topical application; 1 teaspoon oral DMSO daily"},{"t":"Haemorrhoids (adjunct)","tn":"Aambeien (aanvullend)","c":5,"en":"Weak to moderate application alongside standard measures for haemorrhoids.","nl":"Zwak tot matig aanbrengen naast de gewone maatregelen bij aambeien.","d":["20–40% perianal skin twice daily (morning and evening) × 5–7 days; avoid mucosa."],"fr":"Twice daily"},{"t":"IBS abdominal wall pain (adjunct)","tn":"Buikwandpijn bij PDS (aanvullend)","c":5,"en":"Application on tender spots of the belly wall in IBS-related pain.","nl":"Aanbrengen op gevoelige plekken van de buikwand bij pijn door prikkelbare darm.","d":["20–40% to tender points once daily; gut/lifestyle care."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Interstitial cystitis (RIMSO‑50)","tn":"Interstitiële cystitis (RIMSO-50)","c":5,"en":"Describes the officially approved bladder instillation of DMSO for interstitial cystitis, given by a urologist.","nl":"Beschrijft de officieel goedgekeurde blaasspoeling met DMSO bij interstitiële cystitis, door de uroloog."},{"t":"Intestinal Fungal Blockage","tn":"Schimmelblokkade in de darm","c":5,"en":"Oral DMSO in aloe juice for a gut fungal infection causing partial blockage.","nl":"DMSO in aloësap via de mond bij een darmschimmel die een gedeeltelijke verstopping geeft.","d":["Give ½ teaspoon of DMSO in 1 ounce of aloe vera diluted with 2 ounces of water after breakfast and dinner.","Continue for 2 weeks after all symptoms have disappeared — not just until symptoms resolve.","If symptoms return after stopping treatment, resume immediately and continue for a longer period.","Monitor response: vomiting and bowel symptoms should reduce within 3–5 days.","Conventional antifungal medications may be used alongside DMSO for more severe infections."],"fr":"Twice daily (after breakfast and dinner)"},{"t":"Medical devices/solvent (Onyx, Tegress, Viadur)","tn":"Medische hulpmiddelen/oplosmiddel (Onyx, Tegress, Viadur)","c":5,"en":"Notes DMSO's role as a solvent in several approved medical products.","nl":"Wijst op DMSO als oplosmiddel in diverse goedgekeurde medische producten."},{"t":"NSAID-Induced Gastritis – DMSO Treatment","tn":"Maagontsteking door NSAID's – behandeling met DMSO","c":5,"en":"Oral DMSO to heal stomach damage caused by painkillers such as NSAIDs.","nl":"DMSO via de mond om maagschade door pijnstillers zoals NSAID's te herstellen.","d":["Take 1 teaspoon of DMSO in juice or water four times daily while NSAID-induced gastritis symptoms are present.","Continue for 5–7 days or until endoscopic confirmation of healing.","Reduce NSAID use where possible — DMSO treats the damage but does not make NSAID use safe.","Aloe vera juice combined with DMSO provides additional gastric protective and soothing benefit.","Long-term: if NSAIDs must be continued, take 1 teaspoon DMSO in juice once daily as a protective maintenance dose."],"fr":"Four times daily for active gastritis; once daily for maintenance protection"},{"t":"Stress-Induced Gastric Mucosal Injury","tn":"Maagslijmvliesbeschadiging door stress","c":5,"en":"DMSO to prevent and treat stress-related stomach lining damage in critically ill patients; hospital use.","nl":"DMSO tegen stressschade aan het maagslijmvlies bij ernstig zieke patiënten; ziekenhuisgebruik.","d":["For hospitalised trauma patients at risk of stress gastric injury: oral DMSO (1 teaspoon in juice or water) administered 3–4 times daily during the acute hospital phase.","IV administration of DMSO can also be used in severely ill patients — medical procedure only.","Continue until the acute stress period has resolved.","DMSO acts as a free radical scavenger, protecting gastric mucosa from the oxidative stress of trauma, shock, and surgery."],"fr":"3–4 times daily during acute hospital phase"},{"t":"Transdermal carrier","tn":"Drager voor opname via de huid","c":5,"en":"Explains DMSO's ability to carry other substances through the skin, so cleanliness matters.","nl":"Legt uit dat DMSO andere stoffen door de huid meeneemt, waardoor schoon werken essentieel is."},{"t":"Urinary Tract Conditions (Non-IC)","tn":"Urinewegaandoeningen (geen IC)","c":5,"en":"Covers urinary tract complaints beyond interstitial cystitis, like urethral pain.","nl":"Gaat over urinewegklachten buiten interstitiële cystitis, zoals pijn in de plasbuis.","d":["For urethral pain or blockage symptoms: DMSO instillation into the bladder or urethra — medical procedure only.","For pelvic or suprapubic discomfort: topical DMSO at 50–60% applied to the lower abdomen over the bladder area can provide symptomatic relief.","Apply a thin layer to the clean, dry lower abdominal skin, allow to fully absorb, and cover with loose cotton clothing.","For sexual pain related to urethral conditions: use the topical protocol above; allow 24–48 hours off DMSO before sexual activity to reduce odour."],"fr":"Once or twice daily for topical use; bladder instillation per medical schedule"},{"t":"Angina Pectoris & Heart Attack (Adjunct)","tn":"Angina pectoris & hartaanval (aanvullend)","c":6,"en":"Describes South American research on DMSO as a cardiac add-on in heart attack and angina; strictly medical.","nl":"Zuid-Amerikaans onderzoek naar DMSO als hartaanvulling bij infarct en angina pectoris; puur medisch.","d":["DMSO for acute cardiac events is an intravenous medical protocol — not a topical self-treatment.","For ongoing angina management as an adjunct: topical DMSO applied to the chest at 50–60% concentration over the precordial region (left chest area), allowing to absorb fully.","DMSO's vasodilatory effect may provide some symptomatic relief of anginal chest tightness when applied topically.","All cardiac DMSO protocols must be discussed with and supervised by a cardiologist."],"fr":"Topical: once or twice daily for angina symptom support; IV use is emergency/hospital only"},{"t":"Pernio / chilblains","tn":"Wintertenen / winterhanden (pernio)","c":6,"en":"Comfort for chilblains caused by cold-induced blood vessel spasm.","nl":"Verlichting bij wintertenen door vaatkramp in de kou.","d":["30–50% to digits once daily; gradual warming/protection."],"fr":"Once daily"},{"t":"Raynaud‑type symptoms (adjunct)","tn":"Raynaud-achtige klachten (aanvullend)","c":6,"en":"Some find comfort in fingers and toes with Raynaud-type symptoms.","nl":"Sommigen ervaren verlichting in vingers en tenen bij Raynaud-achtige klachten.","d":["20–40% to fingers/toes; thermal protection."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Varicose veins (skin comfort)","tn":"Spataderen (huidcomfort)","c":6,"en":"Only soothes the skin over varicose veins; does not treat the veins themselves.","nl":"Verzacht alleen de huid boven spataderen; de aderen zelf worden niet behandeld.","d":["30–50% to intact skin 1×/day; compression per guidance."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Amyloidosis (Adjunct)","tn":"Amyloïdose (aanvullend)","c":7,"en":"Oral and topical DMSO as an add-on for secondary amyloidosis, the build-up of abnormal proteins; medical context.","nl":"DMSO via mond en huid als aanvulling bij secundaire amyloïdose, de ophoping van afwijkende eiwitten; medische context.","d":["For cutaneous (skin) amyloidosis: apply topical DMSO at 50–70% directly to affected skin lesions once or twice daily. Clinical improvement including flattening of papules and reduced itching reported within 2 weeks.","For systemic secondary amyloidosis: oral DMSO (7–15g per day in divided doses, diluted in juice) has shown improvement in kidney function markers. This must only be undertaken under medical supervision.","For localised bladder amyloidosis: intravesical DMSO instillation has shown positive results (medical procedure).","Monitor urine output, kidney function markers, and organ symptoms regularly during any systemic protocol."],"fr":"Daily (topical); divided oral doses under medical supervision"},{"t":"Ankylosing Spondylitis","tn":"Ziekte van Bechterew","c":7,"en":"Topical use along the spine for ankylosing spondylitis (Bechterew).","nl":"Aanbrengen langs de wervelkolom bij de ziekte van Bechterew.","d":["Cleanse the full back area — removing sweat, fabric, and lotion residues.","Apply a 50–70% DMSO blend to the entire spinal column and paraspinal muscles using a spray for broad coverage.","Allow to settle without rubbing. A warm sensation along the spine is normal.","Optionally apply a warm compress over the area once DMSO has fully dried to enhance anti-inflammatory effect.","Pair with gentle range-of-motion exercises after the product has absorbed.","Apply once in the morning and once in the evening during flare periods; reduce to once daily for maintenance."],"fr":"Twice daily during flares; once daily for maintenance"},{"t":"Bacterial skin infections (adjunct)","tn":"Bacteriële huidinfecties (aanvullend)","c":7,"en":"Helps topical antibiotics and antiseptics penetrate in bacterial skin infections.","nl":"Helpt antibiotica en ontsmettingsmiddelen beter door te dringen bij bacteriële huidinfecties.","d":["20–50% with approved agents; monitor irritation."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Chronic Inflammation – Daily Topical Management","tn":"Chronische ontsteking – dagelijkse behandeling op de huid","c":7,"en":"A twice-daily routine aimed at recurring inflammation hotspots.","nl":"Routine van twee keer per dag voor terugkerende ontstekingsplekken.","d":["Identify 2–3 recurring hotspot areas (e.g., sides of the knees, base of the neck, lower spine, outer hips).","Apply a thin, even layer of DMSO dilution (50% is a comfortable starting point) without rubbing; allow to settle.","For inflammation around major joints or along the spine, extend the application slightly into the surrounding muscles.","Once DMSO is fully dry, place a warm (not hot) compress over the area for 5–10 minutes if tissue feels stiff and resistant.","If the area feels overheated or irritated, use a cool compress instead.","Apply before predictable flare periods: after long sitting, late afternoon, after certain activities, or upon waking.","Use a two-part daily rhythm: once in the morning to set the baseline, once in the evening when tissues tighten.","Wear soft, breathable fabrics after application — avoid friction and heat around treated areas."],"fr":"Twice daily — morning and evening"},{"t":"Cold Sores & Post-Herpetic Neuralgia – DMSO + Colloidal Silver","tn":"Koortslippen & postherpetische neuralgie – DMSO + colloïdaal zilver","c":7,"en":"Pairs DMSO with colloidal silver for cold sores, shingles and post-shingles nerve pain.","nl":"DMSO met colloïdaal zilver bij koortslip, gordelroos en zenuwpijn daarna.","d":["Prepare: combine 30% DMSO in 10–15 ppm colloidal silver or distilled water in a dropper bottle.","Apply over the affected area 2–3 times daily.","Expect: DMSO may initially trigger a stronger outbreak (full expression of the virus) — this is the body detoxing the nerve root. Continue treatment through this phase.","Take 2,000mg vitamin C three times daily throughout treatment.","Take a B-complex vitamin with food at breakfast daily.","Post-herpetic neuralgia (persistent nerve pain after shingles): apply DMSO over the affected dermatome area. A temporary increase in rash is normal and indicates the treatment is working."],"fr":"2–3 times daily"},{"t":"Fungal nail (onychomycosis) adjunct","tn":"Nagelschimmel (onychomycose), aanvullend","c":7,"en":"Same idea as the skin entry: DMSO helps antifungals into the nail.","nl":"Zelfde idee als bij Huid: DMSO helpt schimmelmiddelen de nagel in.","d":["30–50% to nail after filing; plus antifungal."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Fungal skin (tinea) adjunct","tn":"Huidschimmel (tinea), aanvullend","c":7,"en":"Penetration aid for antifungal creams in fungal skin infections.","nl":"Hulpmiddel om schimmelcrèmes beter te laten opnemen bij huidschimmel.","d":["20–40% with antifungal cream."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Herpes labialis / shingles (adjunct)","tn":"Koortslip / gordelroos (aanvullend)","c":7,"en":"An antiviral helper and carrier for cold sores and shingles that also eases discomfort.","nl":"Hulp en drager voor antivirale middelen bij koortslip en gordelroos, die ook het ongemak vermindert.","d":["50–70% to lesion margins 2–3×/day; antivirals per label."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Infections – DMSO + Antibiotic Synergy Protocol","tn":"Infecties – DMSO in combinatie met antibiotica","c":7,"en":"DMSO alongside antibiotics for infections that resist standard treatment; prescribed drugs involved.","nl":"DMSO naast antibiotica bij infecties die niet op gewone behandeling reageren; er zijn receptmiddelen bij betrokken.","d":["For resistant soft-tissue or wound infections: add DMSO topically (50–70%) to the infected area twice daily alongside prescribed antibiotic treatment.","For severe internal infections (osteomyelitis, bone infection): DMSO given intravenously in combination with antibiotics — medical procedure only.","For bladder/urinary infections: 1 teaspoon DMSO in cranberry juice 2–3 times daily alongside antibiotic treatment.","For chronic or recurring infections: after resolution, continue 1 teaspoon DMSO in juice daily for 1–2 weeks as maintenance.","DMSO should always accompany, not replace, appropriate antibiotic therapy."],"fr":"Daily (topical and oral) alongside antibiotic course"},{"t":"Lupus – Weekly Injection & Topical Maintenance Protocol","tn":"Lupus – wekelijkse injectie & onderhoud op de huid","c":7,"en":"A weekly DMSO and vitamin injection plus daily lotion for long-term lupus management; needs a medical professional.","nl":"Wekelijkse injectie met DMSO en vitaminen plus dagelijkse lotion bij lupus op lange termijn; vereist een zorgprofessional.","d":["Weekly intramuscular or intravenous injection of DMSO combined with vitamins — administered by a physician.","Daily topical application of a DMSO lotion to painful joints and inflamed areas — use 50–70% DMSO in a lotion base with aloe vera.","Apply topical lotion to affected joints (hands, wrists, knees) once or twice daily.","Oral DMSO (1 teaspoon in juice or water once daily) may be added as supportive maintenance between injection days.","Monitor kidney function, joint pain levels, and organ function at regular intervals with a rheumatologist."],"fr":"Weekly injections; daily topical application"},{"t":"Lupus Erythematosus (Adjunct)","tn":"Lupus erythematodes (aanvullend)","c":7,"en":"An add-on in systemic lupus, mainly for lupus-related skin problems.","nl":"Aanvulling bij systemische lupus, vooral voor huidklachten.","d":["For lupus skin manifestations (facial rash, lesions): apply diluted DMSO (30–40%) to affected skin areas using a cotton pad or spray. Avoid mucous membranes and eyes.","For lupus interstitial cystitis (bladder involvement): intravesical DMSO instillation — this is a medically supervised procedure identical to the RIMSO-50 protocol for IC.","For joint involvement: apply 50–70% DMSO topically to inflamed joints using the arthritis protocol.","Monitor skin carefully — lupus skin is often highly reactive. Begin at low concentrations (20–30%) and increase only if well tolerated."],"fr":"Daily for topical use; bladder instillation per medical schedule"},{"t":"Scleroderma (Progressive Systemic Sclerosis)","tn":"Sclerodermie (progressieve systemische sclerose)","c":7,"en":"Topical or oral DMSO in scleroderma, aimed at small-nerve pain and slow-healing ulcers.","nl":"DMSO op de huid of via de mond bij sclerodermie, tegen pijn in kleine zenuwen en slecht genezende wondjes.","d":["Apply DMSO topically at 70–80% concentration directly to hardened, ulcerated, or painful skin areas.","For finger, wrist, and hand involvement: soak hands and forearms in a DMSO solution for 15–20 minutes per session.","Allow the product to settle fully before covering the area with loose cotton clothing.","Repeat 1–2 times daily. Benefits include reduced pain, softening of skin, healing of surface ulcers, and improved finger mobility.","Oral DMSO (under medical supervision only): diluted in concentrated juice and crushed ice in divided doses. This route was studied at the Cleveland Clinic for systemic effects.","Monitor skin closely — reduce concentration if irritation, redness, or dryness develops."],"fr":"Once or twice daily — long-term maintenance as needed"},{"t":"Sinus infections (adjunct)","tn":"Bijholteontsteking (aanvullend)","c":7,"en":"Points to the sinusitis entries and advises medical review.","nl":"Verwijst naar de sinusitis-items en raadt medische beoordeling aan.","d":["≤10% intranasal isotonic saline (0.9% salt water) short trials; stop if stinging."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Cancer – DMSO-Hematoxylon Protocol (Historic)","tn":"Kanker – DMSO-hematoxylon (historisch)","c":8,"en":"Recounts a historic cancer treatment combining DMSO with hematoxylon, used by one Houston doctor; not current practice.","nl":"Vertelt over een historische kankerbehandeling met DMSO en hematoxyline van een arts in Houston; geen huidige praktijk.","d":["The Tucker DMSO-hematoxylon protocol is a medical treatment administered by a physician — not a self-treatment protocol.","Treatment involves intravenous or intratumoral administration of a hematoxylon-DMSO compound on an every-other-day basis.","Patients in Tucker's practice reported no nausea or typical chemotherapy side effects.","Treatment is typically given over 18 months, with CEA (cancer marker) blood tests used to monitor response.","DMSO carries hematoxylon across cell membranes into tumour tissue; the compound then acts to normalise abnormal cancer cell function."],"fr":"Every other day — medical administration"},{"t":"Chemo potentiation / tissue protection (historic)","tn":"Versterking van chemo / weefselbescherming (historisch)","c":8,"en":"Historical research into DMSO as a booster for chemotherapy or a protector of healthy tissue.","nl":"Historisch onderzoek naar DMSO als versterker van chemo of als bescherming van gezond weefsel."},{"t":"Leukaemia – DMSO Cell Differentiation (Adjunct)","tn":"Leukemie – celdifferentiatie met DMSO (aanvullend)","c":8,"en":"Describes lab findings that DMSO can make leukaemia cells mature; research context only.","nl":"Beschrijft labbevindingen dat DMSO leukemiecellen kan laten uitrijpen; alleen onderzoekscontext.","d":["DMSO-induced differentiation in leukaemia is a research finding, not an established clinical protocol.","In laboratory studies, DMSO caused leukaemic cells to produce haemoglobin and behave as normal cells.","Clinically, DMSO has been used as a potentiator for chemotherapy in leukaemia — allowing lower doses of toxic chemotherapy agents to be used with equivalent effectiveness.","DMSO combined with cyclophosphamide in Chilean cancer studies showed reduced toxicity of the chemotherapy and improved patient tolerance.","All leukaemia treatment decisions must be made by a qualified haematologist or oncologist."],"fr":"Medical protocol — as directed by oncologist"},{"t":"Radiation protection (historic)","tn":"Bescherming tegen straling (historisch)","c":8,"en":"Historical exploration of DMSO's antioxidant role in protection against radiation.","nl":"Historisch onderzoek naar de antioxiderende rol van DMSO als stralingsbescherming."},{"t":"Topical vitamin C mixes for skin lesions (experimental)","tn":"Vitamine C-mengsels op de huid bij huidletsels (experimenteel)","c":8,"en":"Experimental vitamin C mixtures for skin lesions, based only on case reports; specialist supervision required.","nl":"Experimentele mengsels met vitamine C voor huidafwijkingen, alleen op basis van casussen; begeleiding door een specialist vereist."},{"t":"Canine otitis (Synotic®)","tn":"Oorontsteking bij honden (Synotic®)","c":9,"en":"Notes veterinary ear medicines for dogs that contain DMSO.","nl":"Noemt diergeneeskundige oormiddelen voor honden waar DMSO in zit."},{"t":"Equine swelling and soft‑tissue injuries","tn":"Zwellingen en weke-delenletsel bij paarden","c":9,"en":"Notes licensed veterinary DMSO products for swelling and soft-tissue injuries in horses.","nl":"Noemt geregistreerde DMSO-producten voor zwellingen en wekedelenletsel bij paarden."},{"t":"30-Day Transformation Programme","tn":"30-dagen-transformatieprogramma","c":10,"en":"A four-week programme building up week by week, from technique to mobility and beyond.","nl":"Programma van vier weken dat per week opbouwt, van techniek naar mobiliteit en verder.","d":["WEEK 1 – Skin Comfort & Application Mastery: Master clean-application habits. Choose correct dilutions per body area. Identify which carriers suit your skin. Track which sensations are normal versus irritating.","WEEK 2 – Mobility Expansion & Joint Support: Support one major joint area per day (knees, hips, shoulders, hands, ankles). Pair each application with gentle mobility work. Integrate 5–8 minutes of circulation-boosting activity.","WEEK 3 – Deep Tissue Relief & Tension Unloading: Apply DMSO to large, load-bearing regions. Try enhanced carriers (magnesium or aloe blends). Add heat or castor oil layering. Incorporate brief stretching before bed.","WEEK 4 – Integration, Strength & Long-Term Habits: Create your personal long-term DMSO schedule. Establish a weekly rotation (mobility day, tension day, recovery day). Reduce reactive care and increase proactive support.","DAILY TRACKING: Record area treated, DMSO strength, notes after application, mobility change, pain/discomfort level (0–10), duration of relief, and sleep quality."],"fr":"Daily over 30 days with weekly theme progression"},{"t":"7-Day Relief Plan – Daily Protocol","tn":"7-dagen-verlichtingsplan – dagelijks protocol","c":10,"en":"A one-week daily checklist covering clean application, hydration and movement.","nl":"Dagelijkse checklist voor één week: schoon aanbrengen, voldoende drinken en bewegen.","d":["1. CLEAN SKIN: Wash with mild fragrance-free soap and warm water before every application.","2. CHOOSE YOUR BLEND: Aloe-DMSO for soothing; Magnesium-DMSO for muscle tightness; Water/Hydrosol-DMSO for light routines; Castor oil layered after DMSO for deeper support.","3. APPLY THINLY: A thin film is enough. Apply with clean hands or roll-on; let settle for 1–2 minutes. Avoid touching clothing during this window.","4. ADD CARRIER: After DMSO settles, apply aloe gel, magnesium solution, or castor oil on top.","5. HYDRATE: Drink at least 1.5–2 litres of water daily.","6. MOVEMENT BREAKS: Every 2–3 hours: 10 calf raises, 5 deep breaths, 5 shoulder circles, a 2-minute walk.","7. OPTIONAL SECOND APPLICATION: If discomfort returns, one light secondary application on the specific tight area is permitted.","8. PRODUCT-FREE WINDOW: Keep skin free of lotions, deodorant, makeup, perfume, and oils for 2 hours after DMSO.","9. DAILY COMFORT SCAN: Note whether skin stayed calm, mobility improved, discomfort decreased, or any area felt sensitive.","10. EVENING WIND-DOWN: Rinse or wipe the area; reapply the gentler aloe-DMSO mix if needed; follow with light stretching or a warm compress."],"fr":"Daily for 7 days"},{"t":"Aloe Vera as a DMSO Carrier – Blends, Ratios & Use","tn":"Aloë vera als drager voor DMSO – mengsels, verhoudingen & gebruik","c":10,"en":"A guide to using aloe vera gel as a base for DMSO and choosing a good aloe.","nl":"Gids voor aloëvera-gel als basis voor DMSO en het kiezen van een goede aloë.","d":["CHOOSE THE RIGHT ALOE: High-percentage aloe gel or juice with minimal additives. No synthetic fragrance, no alcohol, no heavy oils, no aggressive thickeners. Avoid alcohol-based aloe — it causes unnecessary stinging with DMSO. Fresh aloe leaf gel works but does not keep long.","BLEND RATIOS: For very sensitive skin or beginners: 70% aloe + 30% DMSO. For a balanced everyday blend: 50% aloe + 50% DMSO. For a stronger DMSO presence still moderated by aloe: 30% aloe + 70% DMSO.","MIXING: Use a glass container and glass or stainless-steel stirrer. Add aloe first, then slowly add DMSO on top. Stir gently — no vigorous shaking or whipping. Never use plastic containers.","APPLICATION: Apply a thin, even layer — just enough to lightly coat the skin. Let settle and dry naturally. No hard rubbing — aggressive rubbing increases sensitivity.","EVERYDAY READY-TO-USE FORMULA: 1 teaspoon DMSO 70% + 2 teaspoons pure aloe gel. Mix gently in a small glass jar. Apply a thin layer to clean skin and allow to dry.","BEST FOR: Knees, shoulders, neck, back, hands, feet, and ankles. Dry or reactive skin. Daily use over the same region. New DMSO users. Large coverage areas. Situations where a gentler, more forgiving experience is desired."],"fr":"Use daily or as needed — aloe is the most sustainable everyday carrier for frequent DMSO use"},{"t":"Application materials","tn":"Materialen voor het aanbrengen","c":10,"en":"Advises simple, clean tools and avoiding plastics that DMSO can attack.","nl":"Raadt eenvoudige, schone hulpmiddelen aan en kunststoffen die DMSO aantast te vermijden."},{"t":"Application Methods – Topical Rubbing, Compresses, Soaks, Sprays & Layering","tn":"Toepassingsmethoden – inwrijven, kompressen, baden, sprays & lagen","c":10,"en":"Overview of the main methods: rubbing in, compresses, soaks, sprays and layering.","nl":"Overzicht van de methodes: inwrijven, kompressen, baden, sprays en in lagen werken.","d":["TOPICAL RUBBING: Apply a small amount (few drops of liquid, pea-sized gel, or thin roll-on pass) to clean fingertips. Use light circular motions — no vigorous rubbing. Allow to air-dry before clothing covers the area. Wash hands unless they were the treatment area.","COMPRESSES: Soak a clean white (undyed) cotton cloth or gauze in your DMSO blend — damp, not dripping. Clean and dry the skin first. Rest the cloth over the area for 5–20 minutes. Warm compresses feel soothing; cool compresses feel refreshing. Only warm the diluent, not the DMSO directly. Allow skin to air-dry fully after removing.","SOAKS: Fill a glass or stainless steel bowl with warm or room-temperature water and your DMSO blend. Swirl gently to distribute. Immerse the hand, foot, or area for 5–15 minutes. Pat dry with a clean towel and allow to finish air-drying. Ideal for hands, feet, and small areas.","SPRAY-ON: Use a glass bottle with stainless steel atomiser. Hold 5–10cm from clean, dry skin and release a fine mist. 1–3 sprays for small areas; 3–5 for medium areas; 5–7 for broad areas. Allow to absorb and air-dry — no need to rub. Avoid synthetic fabric contact until dry.","ROLL-ON: Fill glass bottle two-thirds full. Invert once to wet the roller. Apply 2–4 slow passes for small joints; 4–6 for medium areas; 6–10 for shoulders, thighs, upper back. Light pressure only — do not press hard. Allow to dry before clothing contact.","LAYERING WITH OTHER PRODUCTS: DMSO blend always goes first on clean, completely dry skin. Wait 3–15 minutes until the skin feels dry to the touch. Only then apply the second layer (aloe, unscented moisturiser, or light natural oil). Avoid alcohol, heavy fragrances, essential oils, strong dyes, or exfoliating acids in the same routine."],"fr":"Choose method based on the area, skin sensitivity, and desired experience"},{"t":"Arnica + DMSO – Herbal Pairing for Bruises, Strains & Overworked Tissue","tn":"Arnica + DMSO – kruidencombinatie bij kneuzingen, verrekkingen & overbelast weefsel","c":10,"en":"How to pair alcohol-free arnica gel with DMSO for bruises and overworked muscles.","nl":"Hoe je alcoholvrije arnicagel met DMSO combineert bij blauwe plekken en overbelaste spieren.","d":["CHOOSE THE RIGHT ARNICA: Use an alcohol-free arnica gel or high-quality arnica cream — not arnica oil (too thick) and never arnica with alcohol (causes stinging with DMSO). Choose the simplest ingredient list: no perfumes, essential oils, or menthol.","BLEND RATIOS: For sensitive skin or tender bruising: 80% arnica gel + 20% DMSO. Balanced everyday blend: 70% arnica gel + 30% DMSO. Stronger for dense muscle tension or post-intense training: 50% arnica gel + 50% DMSO.","MIXING: Place measured arnica gel into a small glass jar first. Slowly add DMSO on top. Mix gently with a glass or stainless-steel spoon — a slow fold is enough. The final blend should feel like a light, silky gel.","APPLICATION: Wash the area first. Apply a thin, even layer of the arnica-DMSO gel directly to the tender area — over a bruise, along a strained calf, across a tight forearm, or into muscles surrounding a sore knee or shoulder. Let rest for 1–2 minutes as it absorbs.","POST-ACTIVITY LAYERING METHOD: After physical strain (workout, gardening, hiking, a sudden twist), wash the area, apply the blend lightly, rest for 10 minutes. If the body welcomes it, follow with gentle mobility: slow circles, light stretching, easy range-of-motion movements.","SAFETY: Do not apply on broken skin or open wounds. Keep away from eyes and mouth. Never stack multiple products directly on wet DMSO — apply arnica-DMSO first, let it absorb, then apply other topicals later."],"fr":"After physical strain, bruising, or overexertion — as needed"},{"t":"Calendula + DMSO – Gentle Herbal Pairing for Stressed or Irritated Skin","tn":"Calendula + DMSO – milde kruidencombinatie voor gestreste of geïrriteerde huid","c":10,"en":"Pairing calendula oil or water with DMSO for irritated or stressed skin.","nl":"Calendula-olie of -water samen met DMSO voor geïrriteerde of gestreste huid.","d":["BLEND RATIOS: For a gentle daily blend using calendula-infused oil in an aloe base: 30% calendula-infused oil + 70% aloe vera gel as the carrier base, then add DMSO at 30–50% of the total. For a lighter, more fluid blend using calendula hydrosol: 50% hydrosol + 50% DMSO.","MIXING: Start with a small glass jar. Place aloe or calendula-infused oil in first as a protective buffer. Slowly pour in the DMSO. Stir gently with a stainless-steel or glass utensil.","APPLICATION: Spread a light, even layer across clean skin — just enough for a thin coat. Best for sensitive or repeatedly stressed regions: inner elbow, back of hand, tops of feet, around the knees, or muscles that tighten from daily activity.","BEST TIMING: Evening routines when the body is winding down. Nightly application to a joint or muscle that has carried tension throughout the day. For those needing regular DMSO use who want a sustainable, nurturing ritual rather than a clinical protocol.","PAIRING WITH OTHER CARRIERS: Calendula blends easily with aloe, hydrosols, or a touch of castor oil (layered, not fully mixed) for different consistencies."],"fr":"Daily or as needed — especially for sensitive areas or ongoing routine use"},{"t":"Choosing Quality DMSO – Purity Grades & What to Look For","tn":"Goede DMSO kiezen – zuiverheidsgraden & waar je op let","c":10,"en":"Explains purity grades of DMSO and what to look for when buying.","nl":"Legt de zuiverheidsgraden van DMSO uit en waar je bij aankoop op let.","d":["INDUSTRIAL GRADE — NEVER USE: Designed for manufacturing, degreasing, and chemical processing. May contain solvents, stabilisers, metal traces, and chemical byproducts. If a bottle does not clearly state pharmaceutical or laboratory grade at 99%+ purity, assume it is industrial.","LABORATORY (LAB) GRADE — MINIMUM STANDARD: 99–99.9% pure, filtered carefully, packaged in non-reactive containers. Used in biological research and cellular studies. Acceptable for clean personal use in most wellness communities.","PHARMACEUTICAL GRADE — GOLD STANDARD: 99.9%+ purity, tested for biological contaminants, screened for metals and chemical residues, produced under stricter regulatory standards, packaged in certified non-reactive containers. Preferred when safety is the top priority.","DOCUMENTATION TO LOOK FOR: Certificate of Analysis (COA) confirming purity and testing results per batch. Lot number tracking. Clear labelling at 99.9%+ purity. Glass packaging. No added stabilisers or preservatives.","VISUAL QUALITY: Pure high-grade DMSO is completely colourless and clear, resembling clean water. Free of sediment, floating particles, or haze at room temperature. May form clear needle-like crystals in cool temperatures — this is a sign of purity, not contamination. Crystals dissolve when gently warmed.","REJECT IF: Yellowed colour. Remains cloudy at room temperature. Produces sediment. Emits a harsh chemical odour. Stored in soft or reactive plastics. Unlabelled or vaguely labelled. Any doubt about sourcing."],"fr":"Evaluate each new product or supplier before purchasing or using"},{"t":"Combining with other agents","tn":"Combineren met andere middelen","c":10,"en":"Warns that DMSO drags along whatever is on the skin, so choose companions carefully.","nl":"Waarschuwt dat DMSO alles meeneemt wat op de huid zit; kies combinaties dus zorgvuldig."},{"t":"Detox Support – Daily DMSO Routine","tn":"Ondersteuning bij ontgifting – dagelijkse DMSO-routine","c":10,"en":"A morning-to-evening routine framed as supporting natural detox and the lymph system.","nl":"Dagroutine van ochtend tot avond, gepresenteerd als steun voor natuurlijke ontgifting en de lymfe.","d":["MORNING: Drink 1 glass of warm water (small sips). Do 5–10 min of gentle movement (neck rolls, hip circles). Apply a thin layer of DMSO to a tension zone — upper back, lower back, or ankles. Follow with 10 deep diaphragmatic breaths.","MIDDAY: Drink 1 glass of water or herbal tea. Take a 5–10 min walk or mobility break. Apply DMSO to the lower back or ankles before movement if tissues feel tight.","EVENING: Apply DMSO to tight areas (shoulders, lower back). Follow with a warm bath or foot soak, or a cool cloth based on preference. Wind down with quiet activity — reading, stretching, or breathing.","WEEKLY (1–2×): Go to bed 1–2 hours earlier. Consider a simplified food day to reduce body load. Add an extra sweating session (brisk walk, sauna, or warm bath). Combine DMSO application with a movement flow routine."],"fr":"Daily (morning, midday, evening) with weekly enhancers"},{"t":"Diluting DMSO Correctly – Ratios, Steps & Safe Mixing","tn":"DMSO goed verdunnen – verhoudingen, stappen & veilig mengen","c":10,"en":"A general guide on why and how to dilute DMSO and which liquids to use.","nl":"Algemene uitleg waarom en hoe je DMSO verdunt en met welke vloeistoffen.","d":["WHY DILUTE: Dilution controls how quickly DMSO absorbs, how warm or tingly it feels, how gentle or intense the sensation is, how suitable it is for different skin types, and how smoothly it blends with other ingredients.","SAFE DILUENTS: Distilled water, pure unscented aloe vera gel, magnesium oil, cold-pressed castor oil, or unscented botanical hydrosols. Avoid lotions, fragranced products, essential oil blends with unknown purity, or any product with perfumes or additives.","COMMON CONCENTRATION RANGES: 70% (very common — 70ml DMSO + 30ml distilled water per 100ml). 50% (balanced — 50ml DMSO + 50ml aloe or water). 40% (gentle — 40ml DMSO + 60ml diluent). 25% (very gentle cosmetic blend). 10% (light cosmetic formula).","STEP 1 — PREPARE WORKSPACE: Wipe surface clean. Wash and dry hands thoroughly. Remove all scented products from the area.","STEP 2 — USE NON-REACTIVE CONTAINER: Glass or stainless steel only. No regular plastics.","STEP 3 — ADD DILUENT FIRST: Pour the carrier (water, aloe, oil) into the container first. This is the correct order for preparing dilutions — different from topical layering where DMSO goes on skin first.","STEP 4 — ADD DMSO SLOWLY: Pour gently to avoid splashing. If crystallised, warm in hands or lukewarm water first.","STEP 5 — MIX GENTLY: Use a glass or stainless-steel stirrer. Blend until uniform. Some oil-based blends may separate when resting — this is normal.","STEP 6 — TRANSFER & LABEL: Store in an amber glass bottle. Label with contents, percentage, and preparation date.","GOOD BLEND SIGNS: Clear, uniform, free of particles, consistent smell, stored in a non-reactive bottle. If yellowed, foul-smelling, or cloudy at room temperature — discard and prepare fresh."],"fr":"Follow each time you prepare a new DMSO blend"},{"t":"Dilution & concentration guide","tn":"Gids voor verdunning & concentratie","c":10,"en":"Explains matching strength to skin thickness and sensitivity.","nl":"Legt uit dat de sterkte moet passen bij huiddikte en gevoeligheid.","d":["Face 5–20%, torso/arms 30–50%, legs/feet 50–80%, scars up to 70%.","Avoid >15% on fresh stitches; avoid open wounds."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"DIY DMSO Roll-Ons, Sprays & Compresses – How to Prepare Your Own","tn":"Zelf DMSO-rollers, sprays & kompressen maken","c":10,"en":"How to prepare your own roll-ons, sprays and compresses.","nl":"Hoe je zelf rollers, sprays en kompressen klaarmaakt.","d":["MATERIALS: Glass is essential — amber glass roll-on bottles (10–30ml), fine-mist amber glass sprayer (30–60ml), or a small glass bowl for compresses. Stainless steel roller balls or DMSO-compatible HDPE inserts for roll-ons. Ensure all tools are clean, dry, and fragrance-free before use.","PREPARE YOUR BLEND: Choose your dilution ratio (70/30, 50/50, or 30/70 DMSO to carrier). Measure carrier liquid first (aloe, magnesium solution, distilled water, or hydrosol), then add DMSO. Stir gently — DMSO does not need vigorous mixing.","FILLING A ROLL-ON: Fill the bottle two-thirds full to prevent overflow. Secure the stainless steel roller ball firmly. Invert the bottle once to wet the roller mechanism. Shake lightly before each use if the blend contains aloe or oils that may separate.","FILLING A SPRAY: Transfer the completed dilution into the glass fine-mist sprayer. Ensure the tube and nozzle are clean. Test with 1–2 pumps before use. Hold 5–10cm from skin and use a fine mist — not a direct stream.","PREPARING A COMPRESS: Pour your prepared dilution into a shallow glass dish. Soak a piece of clean, white (undyed) gauze or cotton cloth. Lightly wring out so it is damp but not dripping. Place against clean, dry skin for 5–20 minutes.","LABELLING & STORAGE: Label each container with contents, concentration, and preparation date. Store in amber glass, away from heat and sunlight. Discard and prepare fresh if the blend becomes cloudy, discoloured, or develops an unusual odour."],"fr":"Prepare blends fresh as needed — most blends remain stable for several weeks in sealed glass"},{"t":"DMSO + Castor Oil – Layering for Deep Sustained Support","tn":"DMSO + ricinusolie – in lagen voor diepe, langdurige ondersteuning","c":10,"en":"Using DMSO and castor oil one after another, not premixed, for deep support.","nl":"DMSO en ricinusolie na elkaar gebruiken, niet vooraf gemengd, voor diepere werking.","d":["UNDERSTAND THE PAIRING: DMSO and castor oil do not form a permanent blend (DMSO is water-soluble; castor oil is not). Always work with them in layers — DMSO first, castor oil second.","CHOOSE DMSO STRENGTH: For sensitive skin or first experiments: 30% DMSO / 70% distilled water. For general everyday use: 50% DMSO / 50% distilled water. For experienced users and denser tissues (hips, lower back): 70% DMSO / 30% distilled water.","BASIC LAYERING METHOD: 1. Prepare skin — clean, fragrance-free, completely dry. 2. Apply a thin layer of DMSO (½ teaspoon or a few spray/roll-on passes for a palm-sized area). Let sit 1–2 minutes until no longer visibly wet. 3. Gently spread 1–2 teaspoons of cold-pressed castor oil over the same area to form a rich, glistening layer.","CASTOR OIL PACK WITH DMSO UNDERLAYER: 1. Clean and dry the skin. 2. Apply thin DMSO layer and let sit 1–2 minutes. 3. Massage castor oil generously over the same region. 4. Place a piece of clean cotton or flannel over the oiled skin. 5. Add a gentle heat source (warm water bottle or low heat pad) on top. 6. Rest for 20–45 minutes.","BEST AREAS: Lower back and sacrum, hips and SI joints, tight shoulders and upper back, knees and ankles, abdomen.","IF PRE-MIXING A SMALL AMOUNT: Combine 1 part DMSO (70% solution) with 2–3 parts castor oil in a small glass bowl immediately before use. Stir gently — it will not be perfectly uniform but is usable for a single session."],"fr":"As needed — particularly for deep tissue support, evening sessions, or castor pack routines"},{"t":"DMSO + Castor Oil Combination Protocol","tn":"DMSO + ricinusolie – combinatieprotocol","c":10,"en":"Combines DMSO with hexane-free castor oil for rheumatic pain, scars and tendon problems.","nl":"DMSO met hexaanvrije ricinusolie bij reumatische pijn, littekens en peesklachten.","d":["Apply a thin layer of hexane-free castor oil over the clean, dry treatment area.","Pat 80–90% DMSO over the castor oil and allow to work in for about 10 minutes. The castor oil dilutes the DMSO to a skin-tolerable level.","Leave on or wash off after 20–30 minutes using a baking soda solution (1 tsp baking soda dissolved in ½ cup water).","For feet: put on clean cotton socks after treatment to move around freely.","A hot water bottle placed over the treated area (wrapped in a towel) enhances penetration, though the DMSO itself will warm the castor oil.","Use once or twice daily for chronic conditions."],"fr":"Once or twice daily"},{"t":"DMSO + CBD Oil Combination – Pain & Nervous System Support","tn":"DMSO + CBD-olie – ondersteuning bij pijn & zenuwstelsel","c":10,"en":"Pairs CBD oil with DMSO for pain, tension and nervous-system calm.","nl":"CBD-olie gecombineerd met DMSO bij pijn, spanning en een onrustig zenuwstelsel.","d":["Use a high-quality CBD extract in liquid form. Blend with 50% DMSO solution.","Apply 15ml of the total mixture to clean temples, the back of the neck over the spine, and the soles of the feet for maximum nervous system absorption.","Start with 15ml total volume and observe effects for 2 hours before increasing.","If groggy the next morning, perform a liver detox (castor oil pack over the liver for 20 minutes daily) or apply the treatment earlier in the evening and use less.","For pain: rub the CBD-DMSO blend over the painful area in addition to the neurological application sites."],"fr":"Once daily (evening recommended); reduce if morning grogginess occurs"},{"t":"DMSO + Colloidal Silver Combination – Infection Protocol","tn":"DMSO + colloïdaal zilver – protocol bij infecties","c":10,"en":"Combines colloidal silver with DMSO as a claimed antibacterial and antifungal mix.","nl":"Colloïdaal zilver met DMSO als veronderstelde bacterie- en schimmelremmende combinatie.","d":["TOPICAL / WOUNDS: Mix pharmaceutical-grade DMSO with 10–15 ppm colloidal silver in a 50:50 ratio. Apply to infected or inflamed skin 2–3 times daily.","MOUTHWASH: Use the 50:50 mixture as a mouthwash for gum disease, tooth infections, or oral bacteria. Swish for 2 minutes and spit thoroughly.","EAR DROPS: 5ml DMSO + 45ml 15 ppm colloidal silver in a glass dropper bottle (10% DMSO). Apply 1–2 drops in each ear once or twice daily. Continue a few days after symptoms clear.","SINUS RINSE: Add 50:50 DMSO-colloidal silver mixture to a saline neti pot solution for sinus infections, polyps, or chronic inflammation.","ORAL (stomach/gut): Add 5ml of the 50:50 mixture to 60ml (2 oz) of distilled water and drink for stomach infections, SIBO, or ulcers."],"fr":"2–3 times daily (topical); once or twice daily (ear drops)"},{"t":"DMSO + Essential Oil Combinations Guide","tn":"Gids voor combinaties van DMSO met etherische oliën","c":10,"en":"How DMSO greatly increases skin absorption of essential oils, which calls for caution.","nl":"DMSO verhoogt de opname van etherische oliën sterk via de huid, dus voorzichtigheid is nodig.","d":["GENERAL RULE: Use 1–2 drops of essential oil per 10 drops of 80% DMSO per application. DMSO requires much less essential oil to achieve the effect.","WINTERGREEN (inflammation & pain): 1–2 drops in 10 drops of 80% DMSO. Apply to inflamed joints or painful muscles.","PEPPERMINT (headache, nerve pain, sciatica): 1 drop in 10 drops of 80% DMSO. Rub over temples for headache or over sciatic nerve path for nerve pain.","BLACK PEPPER (lymphatic, leg swelling, water retention): 1–2 drops in 10 drops of 80% DMSO. Massage upward from the bottom of each leg to encourage lymphatic drainage.","SWEET BIRCH or CLARY SAGE (muscle relaxation): 1–2 drops (or 1 drop of each) in 10 drops of 80% DMSO. Massage into tight muscles up to twice daily.","Apply to clean skin only. Do not use on children, pregnant, or nursing women."],"fr":"As needed for acute pain; up to twice daily for ongoing conditions"},{"t":"DMSO + MSM Combined Internal Protocol","tn":"DMSO + MSM – gecombineerd protocol voor inname","c":10,"en":"Taking DMSO and MSM together internally for systemic sulphur support.","nl":"DMSO en MSM samen innemen voor ondersteuning met zwavel van binnenuit.","d":["START LOW: Begin with 500mg MSM twice daily (capsule or powder). Work up slowly over 4–7 days to ½ teaspoon twice daily.","FOR SPECIFIC CONDITIONS: Increase to 1 teaspoon twice daily. Can be taken with or without food.","COMBINED WITH DMSO: Take ½–1 teaspoon of DMSO diluted in 150ml (5 oz) of water or juice, followed immediately by your MSM dose.","FOR GUT HEALING / PARASITE CONTROL: The DMSO opens access for the MSM to penetrate the intestinal lining, assisting gut repair and making conditions unfavourable for parasites.","ODOUR ALTERNATIVE: To minimise DMSO breath odour, use MSM internally and DMSO only topically."],"fr":"Twice daily"},{"t":"DMSO + Vitamin C Cancer Prevention Protocol","tn":"DMSO + vitamine C – protocol ter preventie van kanker","c":10,"en":"An author's preventive plan pairing oral DMSO with buffered vitamin C; framed as prevention, not treatment.","nl":"Preventieplan van een auteur met DMSO via de mond en gebufferde vitamine C; als preventie gebracht, niet als behandeling.","d":["Take 5g of buffered vitamin C (calcium ascorbate, potassium ascorbate, or sodium ascorbate — never ascorbic acid alone for large doses) twice daily.","Take 1 teaspoon of 99.995% DMSO diluted in 150ml (5 oz) of distilled water or juice, 10 minutes before the second dose of vitamin C.","The DMSO must be taken on an empty stomach: 2 hours after the last meal, and no food for 2 hours after.","BUILD UP SLOWLY: Day 1 = ¼ tsp; Day 2 = ½ tsp; Day 3 = ¼ tsp; Day 4 onward = 1 tsp.","Use this protocol for 2 weeks, 4 times per year — ideally at season changes.","Eat a whole-food diet and avoid refined sugar, white flour, sodas, and synthetic sugars during the protocol."],"fr":"Daily for 2-week cycles, 4 times per year"},{"t":"DMSO as a Carrier Agent – What Can & Cannot Be Used","tn":"DMSO als drager – wat wel en niet kan","c":10,"en":"Explains the carrier effect and which companion ingredients are and aren't suitable.","nl":"Legt het drager-effect uit en welke combinaties wel en niet geschikt zijn.","d":["CARRIER MECHANISM: DMSO slips through the skin's protective barrier by softening the spaces between surface cells, taking dissolved ingredients with it. The skin closes behind it, but during this window absorption is dramatically more efficient.","SAFE COMPANION INGREDIENTS: Pure aloe vera gel (no alcohol, no fragrance), distilled water, pure unscented hydrosols, magnesium chloride solutions, high-quality alcohol-free herbal extracts (arnica, calendula), and cold-pressed castor oil (layered after DMSO, not fully mixed).","APPLICATION SEQUENCE: Apply DMSO first as a thin even layer. Allow 1 minute to settle. Apply the companion ingredient second. DMSO opens the path; the second ingredient follows.","NEVER USE WITH DMSO: Synthetic fragrances, alcohol, petroleum derivatives, strong essential oils, artificial preservatives, colours, dyes, perfumes, commercial body lotions, or any product with an unknown ingredient list.","GOLDEN RULE: If you wouldn't want it passing deeper into the skin, keep it out of your blend.","CLEAN SKIN IS NON-NEGOTIABLE: Even residues from fragrant soap, conditioner, laundry detergent on clothing, deodorant, sunscreen, or scented lotion from earlier in the day can be carried inward by DMSO."],"fr":"Apply this knowledge before every DMSO blend preparation"},{"t":"DMSO Concentrations Guide – What Strength to Use","tn":"Gids voor DMSO-concentraties – welke sterkte gebruiken","c":10,"en":"Guidance on choosing a suitable strength per body area and complaint.","nl":"Richtlijnen voor de passende sterkte per lichaamsdeel en klacht.","d":["20–30% — Sensitive skin, face, children, eyes (as eye drops in saline), ears. Gentle and appropriate for long-term regular use.","40–50% — General body use, sinuses (neti pot), wounds, standard pain management. The all-purpose range for most people.","60–70% — Joint pain, arthritis, muscle injuries, carpal tunnel, most pain conditions. Effective without significant skin thickening.","80% — Bursitis, tendinitis, chronic injury sites, castor oil protocols. Maximum recommended for repeated home use on most skin.","90–99.995% — Tendinitis (specific supervised protocol), small wounds, scar tissue, cavities. Use sparingly; causes skin thickening and peeling with repeated use on the same area.","Always patch test on the inside of the wrist before first use. Redness fading within 5–20 minutes is normal.","If skin irritation occurs, reduce concentration by 10% and retest. Never start at maximum concentration."],"fr":"As per condition; concentrations listed are for each application"},{"t":"DMSO Formats – Liquid vs Gel vs Roll-On","tn":"DMSO-vormen – vloeistof, gel of roller","c":10,"en":"Compares liquid, gel and roll-on forms and their pros and cons.","nl":"Vergelijkt vloeistof, gel en roller met hun voor- en nadelen.","d":["LIQUID DMSO — Fast, potent, most versatile: Absorbs very quickly. Easy to dilute precisely. Ideal for compresses, targeted applications, large or small areas, and mixing with aloe, magnesium, or oils. Demands disciplined skin cleanliness. Not ideal for very sensitive skin unless diluted.","DMSO GEL — Gentle, controlled, beginner-friendly: Contains high-purity DMSO plus a natural thickening agent (often aloe vera). Slower absorbing, less likely to run or drip. Ideal for delicate or curved body regions. Helpful when a longer contact time is desired. May leave a slightly tacky finish.","ROLL-ON DMSO — Most convenient, lowest mess: Glass bottle with stainless steel or HDPE roller ball. No hand-to-product contact. Perfect for on-the-go use and areas like hands, neck, shoulders, and fingers. Reduces contamination risk. Choose roll-ons with non-reactive components (glass + stainless steel) — avoid cheap plastic balls.","CHOOSE BASED ON: Craving simplicity → Roll-on. Want control and versatility → Liquid. Seek gentleness → Gel. Many long-term users keep all three on hand.","QUALITY IN ANY FORMAT: Glass packaging. Clear labelling. 99.9% purity. No added fragrances. Transparent sourcing. Clean thickeners (for gels). Stainless steel or HDPE roll heads."],"fr":"Use as a format selection guide when purchasing or preparing DMSO"},{"t":"DMSO Odour Management – Wintergreen & Hydrogen Peroxide Methods","tn":"DMSO-geur beperken – met wintergroen & waterstofperoxide","c":10,"en":"Advanced tips for reducing DMSO's odour, using wintergreen or peroxide methods.","nl":"Geavanceerde tips tegen de DMSO-geur, met wintergreen of waterstofperoxide.","d":["WINTERGREEN MOUTHWASH: Add 1 drop of 100% pure wintergreen essential oil to 30ml (1 oz) of water. Swish for 30 seconds and spit. Use as needed to control breath odour. Do not swallow.","HYDROGEN PEROXIDE MOUTHWASH: Add 5 drops of 3% food-grade hydrogen peroxide to 30ml of pure water. Swish a few times daily while using DMSO internally. Always spit — never swallow.","TOPICAL INSTEAD OF ORAL: Using DMSO topically and taking MSM internally (in place of oral DMSO) significantly reduces breath odour, as topical metabolism produces less DMS than oral.","COPPER AWARENESS: People with higher copper levels smell the DMS odour more strongly. If those around you are very sensitive to the smell, suggest they take zinc, manganese, and iron to balance excess copper."],"fr":"As needed for odour control"},{"t":"DMSO Storage & Shelf Life","tn":"DMSO bewaren & houdbaarheid","c":10,"en":"How to store DMSO to keep it pure and stable: temperature, light and containers.","nl":"Hoe je DMSO zuiver en stabiel bewaart: temperatuur, licht en verpakking.","d":["TEMPERATURE: Store at room temperature (20–25°C / 68–77°F). DMSO crystallises below ~18.5°C (65°F) — this is normal and does not reduce potency. Gently warm crystals in your hands or in lukewarm water. Never use boiling water, microwaves, or direct heat.","LIGHT EXPOSURE: DMSO is not photosensitive and does not degrade under normal light. Amber or dark glass bottles are recommended to help stabilise temperature, not to block light.","AIR EXPOSURE: DMSO is hygroscopic (attracts moisture from air). Keep the bottle tightly sealed. Open only when needed. Never pour unused portions back into the bottle. Keep cap threads clean.","CONTAMINATION PREVENTION: Use clean, dry hands and dedicated tools. Never 'double-dip' tools that have touched skin. Wipe the bottle opening occasionally with a lint-free cloth. Treat the bottle as a long-term partner — not a disposable item.","SHELF LIFE: Unopened high-purity DMSO is commonly stable for 3–5 years. Once opened, 2–3 years is typical if contamination and moisture exposure are avoided.","SIGNS OF COMPROMISED QUALITY: Unusual coloration, persistent cloudiness at warm temperatures, unfamiliar odours, or sediment that does not dissolve when warmed.","IDEAL STORAGE LOCATIONS: Bedroom cabinets, hallway closets, pantry shelves, or kitchen cabinets away from heat sources. Avoid under-sink cabinets, garages, areas near heaters, and bathrooms with high humidity.","TRAVEL: Use a tightly sealed glass bottle, padded to prevent breakage. For short-term travel, DMSO-compatible HDPE containers may be used if clearly labelled and leak-proof. Avoid leaving DMSO in hot cars or exposed to extreme temperature swings."],"fr":"Follow these guidelines at all times when storing DMSO"},{"t":"Healing Crisis & Detoxification Reactions – Management Guide","tn":"Genezingscrisis & ontgiftingsreacties – hoe ermee om te gaan","c":10,"en":"How to recognise and handle a \"healing crisis\" or detox reaction after starting.","nl":"Hoe je een 'genezingscrisis' of ontgiftingsreactie na de start herkent en opvangt.","d":["START SLOWLY: Begin with a low concentration (20–30%) or a very small oral dose (¼ teaspoon). Increase gradually over 4–7 days.","If you experience headache, nausea, fatigue, skin rash, or mood changes, do not increase the dose. Hold at the current level until symptoms pass.","Drink 2–3 litres of pure distilled or reverse osmosis water daily to help flush released toxins through the kidneys.","REST AND FASTING: During a significant detox reaction, reducing food intake and resting allows the liver to process toxins more efficiently.","NATURAL ANTIHISTAMINE (for histamine reactions — itching, hives, swelling): Mix 2 tablespoons sodium bicarbonate + 1 tablespoon potassium bicarbonate. Dissolve ½ teaspoon in warm water and drink. A second dose can be taken 20–30 minutes later if symptoms persist. Do not repeat for 24 hours.","STOP DMSO IMMEDIATELY if you experience trouble breathing, facial swelling, or severe hives — these are serious reactions requiring medical attention."],"fr":"Management protocol as needed during healing crisis"},{"t":"Hydrosols & Distilled Water as DMSO Carriers","tn":"Hydrolaten & gedestilleerd water als drager voor DMSO","c":10,"en":"Using hydrosols and distilled water as light, clean bases for DMSO.","nl":"Hydrolaten en gedestilleerd water als lichte, schone basis voor DMSO.","d":["WHY THESE CARRIERS: Hydrosols carry just enough plant character to feel soothing without overwhelming the skin. Distilled water removes all minerals, chlorine, and residues for the purest possible base. Both create light, quick-drying blends with no residue.","BLEND RATIOS: Gentle blend for sensitive skin or beginners: 25% DMSO + 75% hydrosol or distilled water. Balanced everyday body use: 50% DMSO + 50% carrier. Stronger but still moderated: 70% DMSO + 30% distilled water.","MIXING: Start with hydrosol or distilled water in a glass bottle first, then slowly add DMSO. Gentle swirl or stir with glass or stainless-steel spoon. Results in a clear, fluid solution suitable for a fine-mist sprayer, roll-on, or glass dropper.","BEST HYDROSOL PAIRINGS: Rose hydrosol — nurturing tone, ideal for neck or chest applications. Lavender or chamomile hydrosol — calming, ideal for evening routines. Rosemary hydrosol — grounded, warming tone for upper back and shoulder tension. Peppermint hydrosol — cooling and invigorating for neck, forearms, and tired legs.","IMPORTANT: Always use hydrosols, not essential oils. Rosemary or peppermint essential oils are too potent to pair directly with DMSO and should never be mixed with it. Hydrosols are mild enough when diluted properly.","BEST AREAS: Neck, upper chest (avoiding mucous membranes), arms, forearms, lower legs, back of hands, upper back. Anywhere the skin is thinner or more reactive."],"fr":"As needed — especially for sensitive skin, daily use, or light on-the-go applications"},{"t":"Hygiene & Application Rules – The Clean Application Mindset","tn":"Hygiëne & regels bij het aanbrengen – schoon werken","c":10,"en":"The full hygiene framework: preparing the skin, clean hands and tools.","nl":"Het complete hygiënekader: huid voorbereiden, schone handen en materialen.","d":["PREPARE SKIN: Wash with mild, fragrance-free soap and warm water. Remove every trace of deodorant, lotion, perfume, makeup, sunscreen, oils, and detergent residue. Pat completely dry.","CLEAN HANDS & TOOLS: Freshly washed, scent-free hands only. Use glass roll-ons, sterile gauze, clean cotton pads, or glass droppers. Avoid all plastics unless verified DMSO-safe.","APPLY DMSO FIRST: Spread a thin, even layer — just enough to lightly coat the area. Allow 30–90 seconds to begin absorbing before adding any carrier.","LAYER CARRIER SECOND: After DMSO settles, apply your carrier: aloe vera (cools, softens, hydrates), magnesium solution (muscular support), castor oil (slow-moisturising finish), or hydrosol/distilled water (light and fast-drying). Never reverse this order.","PROTECT THE AREA: For 20–30 minutes after application, avoid touching face or eyes, leaning on surfaces, or covering the area with tight or synthetic clothing. If dressing, choose clean cotton or linen in unscented detergent.","ENVIRONMENTAL AWARENESS: Avoid applying near perfumes, aerosol sprays, chemical cleaners, or recently scented fabrics. A clean room and clean air are part of the protocol.","CONTAINERS: Mix and store only in glass, stainless steel, or HDPE plastic rated for solvents. Label bottles clearly with contents, percentage, and date.","ADJUST STRENGTH THOUGHTFULLY: If the area feels too warm, tight, or dry, dilute to 30–50% DMSO. If the effect feels too mild, gradually increase up to 70%. Let skin adapt before changing the formula.","PATCH TEST: Whenever introducing a new carrier or botanical ingredient, test on a small area first. Discontinue if persistent redness or irritation occurs."],"fr":"Follow before every DMSO application"},{"t":"Magnesium Oil as a DMSO Carrier – Blends, Ratios & Muscle Support","tn":"Magnesiumolie als drager voor DMSO – mengsels, verhoudingen & spierondersteuning","c":10,"en":"Pairing magnesium oil with DMSO for muscle support.","nl":"Magnesiumolie samen met DMSO voor ondersteuning van de spieren.","d":["CHOOSE THE RIGHT MAGNESIUM: Magnesium chloride flakes dissolved in water, or a ready-made solution with as few extras as possible. No alcohol, no menthol, no synthetic fragrance, no heavy essential oils.","BLEND RATIOS: Mild introductory blend: 70% magnesium solution + 30% DMSO. More noticeable working feel: 50% magnesium + 50% DMSO. Experienced users with known skin tolerance: 30% magnesium + 70% DMSO. If skin stings or itches excessively, increase magnesium portion or add a small amount of aloe.","MIXING: Use a small glass bottle or jar and glass or stainless-steel stirrer. Pour magnesium solution in first, then slowly add DMSO. Gentle swirl or slow stir — no vigorous shaking.","APPLICATION: Apply to clean, dry skin (no fresh shaving, no heavy lotions). A light mist or thin film is all that is needed — do not rub in. Allow 1–2 minutes to absorb. Then introduce movement: flex and point feet for calves, slow shoulder circles, gentle hip tilts for lower back.","STARTER FORMULA: 1 teaspoon DMSO 70% + 2 teaspoons magnesium solution. Mix gently in a small glass container. Apply a thin layer to clean skin. Allow to absorb before dressing or lying down.","BEST TIMES: After a workout for dense, fatigued muscles. Before bed for restless or heavy legs. In the evening for lower back fatigue from prolonged sitting or standing."],"fr":"As needed — particularly after physical exertion or in the evening"},{"t":"Maintaining DMSO Results Long-Term","tn":"DMSO-resultaten op lange termijn behouden","c":10,"en":"How to keep the gains once a structured DMSO routine is finished.","nl":"Hoe je de resultaten vasthoudt nadat een vaste DMSO-routine is afgerond.","d":["ANCHOR DAYS: Choose 2–3 fixed days per week for a quick DMSO routine — as normal as brushing your teeth. This prevents stiffness from returning and stops mild tension from escalating.","EARLY INTERVENTION: Apply DMSO at the first whisper of discomfort — the familiar tightness in the neck after a long workday, heat building in a knee after a walk, or dull weight in the lower back after prolonged sitting. Catching tension early often resolves it before it becomes louder.","SIMPLIFIED MAINTENANCE BLENDS: A light distilled-water blend or a roll-on with 50–70% DMSO is usually sufficient for weekly maintenance. Bring back aloe, magnesium, or castor-oil layering for deeper care after demanding days or during seasonal stress.","MOVEMENT: Even 5 minutes of gentle mobility after applying DMSO helps preserve fluidity. Think of it as lubricating your joints — a little movement paired with topical support keeps everything warm and responsive.","NIGHTTIME MAINTENANCE: Continue using a nighttime routine once or twice a week, especially during stressful periods. A small application to the feet, calves, or shoulders before bed prevents restless episodes from returning.","CONTINUITY OVER PERFECTION: Life will interrupt your routines. The goal is not to do everything every day — it is to avoid long gaps that undo progress. Even a single weekly session keeps progress steady. Returning to 3 days of targeted use after a break is usually enough to re-establish balance."],"fr":"Ongoing — 2–3 times per week minimum for maintenance after completing a programme"},{"t":"Managing the DMSO Garlic-Like Odour","tn":"De knoflookachtige geur van DMSO beperken","c":10,"en":"Why DMSO causes a garlic-like smell and practical ways to limit it.","nl":"Waarom DMSO een knoflookachtige geur geeft en hoe je die beperkt.","d":["UNDERSTAND THE CAUSE: DMSO metabolises into dimethyl sulphide (DMS), a harmless volatile compound released through the skin and breath. The odour is temporary and not a sign of danger.","REDUCE APPLICATION AREA: Smaller, localised applications produce far less odour than large full-area coatings.","ADJUST CONCENTRATION: Use 50–70% dilution rather than 90–100%. Use distilled water, aloe, or a hydrosol as carrier.","TRY A HONEY BLEND: Mix 70% DMSO with 30% clean filtered or pasteurised honey. Use only pasteurised or medical-grade honey — raw honey with spores is not recommended.","TIMING: Apply DMSO in the evening so the body can metabolise it before social interactions the next day. Shower the next morning with mild natural soap.","HYDRATION: Drink water consistently — volatile sulphur compounds disperse more evenly and less intensely when the body is well hydrated.","DIET ON APPLICATION DAYS: Reduce high-sulphur foods (garlic, onions, eggs, broccoli, cabbage). Add more fresh fruits, leafy greens, and water-rich vegetables.","FOOT APPLICATION: Applying DMSO to the feet (followed by cotton socks) gives good comfort while keeping odour barely noticeable."],"fr":"Apply these strategies whenever DMSO odour is a concern"},{"t":"Natural Antihistamine for DMSO Reactions","tn":"Natuurlijk antihistaminicum bij DMSO-reacties","c":10,"en":"A simple natural remedy for itching or hives as a reaction to DMSO.","nl":"Een eenvoudig natuurlijk middel tegen jeuk of bultjes als reactie op DMSO.","d":["PREPARE: Mix 2 tablespoons sodium bicarbonate (baking soda — not baking powder) + 1 tablespoon potassium bicarbonate (from a compounding pharmacy; cream of tartar can substitute if needed). Store in an airtight jar.","ORAL USE: Dissolve ½ teaspoon of the mixture completely in warm water and drink. Symptoms should resolve fairly rapidly.","SECOND DOSE: If symptoms have not fully resolved after 20–30 minutes, take a second dose. Do not repeat for 24 hours.","TOPICAL USE: Mix the powder into a paste and rub onto the reacting skin area. Leave on until it dissolves naturally.","If you experience difficulty breathing or facial swelling, seek emergency medical help immediately — this is beyond antihistamine management."],"fr":"As needed for reactions; maximum twice per 24-hour period"},{"t":"Nebulising precautions","tn":"Voorzorgen bij vernevelen","c":10,"en":"Precautions for inhalation: only extremely weak in saline, and some devices may be damaged.","nl":"Voorzorgen bij vernevelen: alleen extreem verdund in zoutoplossing, en sommige apparaten kunnen beschadigen.","d":["Start 1–3 drops in 10–20 ml saline; stop if burning/tightness.","No essential oils with DMSO for inhalation."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Oral use basics","tn":"Basis van inname via de mond","c":10,"en":"Oral use only very dilute, expect taste and odour, and consult a clinician first.","nl":"Innemen alleen sterk verdund; reken op smaak en geur en overleg eerst met een arts.","d":["≤20% total; ½–1 tsp in large glass of water after food; short trials.","Avoid if GI bleeding; review meds/interactions."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Overuse Response & Skin Reset Protocol","tn":"Bij overgebruik – herstel van de huid","c":10,"en":"What to do when too much has been applied and how to let the skin recover.","nl":"Wat te doen bij te veel aanbrengen en hoe je de huid laat herstellen.","d":["IMMEDIATE STEPS: Stop applying DMSO immediately. Rinse the area with lukewarm water and a mild, fragrance-free cleanser — do not scrub. Pat dry with a clean towel. Avoid hot water, exfoliants, or alcohol wipes.","SOOTHE: Apply pure aloe vera gel (no alcohol or strong additives) in a thin layer. Repeat every few hours if the area still feels tight or warm.","COOL IF OVERHEATED: Apply a cool compress (soft cloth in cold water) for 5–10 minutes if skin feels overheated or reactive.","BARRIER REPAIR: Apply a simple unscented moisturiser 4–6 hours after redness or sensitivity — not sooner, as residual DMSO may still be active.","REST THE AREA: Avoid tight clothing, heat, friction, and additional topical products for 24 hours.","SKIN RESET (48–72 HOURS): Stop DMSO entirely. Apply aloe vera gel twice daily. Switch to cotton fabrics washed without fragrance or softeners. Take warm (not hot) showers; pat dry rather than rub.","RESUME CAREFULLY: Restart at a lighter concentration (25–50%) and smaller application area. Build back up gradually."],"fr":"As needed when overuse symptoms appear"},{"t":"Skin Irritation Guide – Redness, Dryness & Sensitivity Spots","tn":"Gids bij huidirritatie – roodheid, droogheid & gevoelige plekken","c":10,"en":"Handling the common skin reactions: redness, dryness and sensitive spots.","nl":"Omgaan met de gebruikelijke huidreacties: roodheid, droogheid en gevoelige plekken.","d":["REDNESS – OBSERVE: A soft pink flush fading within 10–20 minutes is a normal vascular response. If the skin becomes hot, blotchy, swollen, or sharply uncomfortable, act immediately.","REDNESS – RESPOND: Rinse with cool water (no soap, no scrubbing). Apply pure aloe vera gel, calendula cream, or chamomile hydrosol. Avoid heavy oils immediately. Reduce concentration by 10–20% and use a 'place-and-spread' technique rather than rubbing.","DRYNESS – PREVENT: Replenish moisture once DMSO has fully absorbed — apply aloe vera or a fragrance-free moisturiser. If recurring, reduce concentration. Avoid long hot showers and harsh soaps on application days.","DRYNESS – LONGER TERM: Layer castor oil or jojoba later in the day to lock moisture in for regularly treated areas.","SENSITIVITY SPOTS – IDENTIFY: Inner arms, sides of the neck, chest, under the knees, and ankles react more sharply — use lower concentrations in these zones.","SENSITIVITY SPOTS – MANAGE: Reduce concentration in reactive zones. Use a thin, even film rather than pressing or rubbing. Give reactive spots a 24–48 hour break while continuing treatment elsewhere.","BUILD A BODY MAP: Note which areas are more reactive and use lighter blends there consistently."],"fr":"Apply this guidance whenever skin reactions occur"},{"t":"Skin preparation & patch testing","tn":"Huid voorbereiden & testen op een klein plekje","c":10,"en":"Clean, residue-free skin and a small test spot to lower the risks.","nl":"Schone huid zonder resten en een klein testplekje om risico's te verkleinen.","d":["Wash with mild soap; dry thoroughly.","patch test (apply to a small area and wait 24 hours) 10–20% for 24 h before wider application."],"fr":"As directed / as tolerated"},{"t":"Storage & handling","tn":"Bewaren & hanteren","c":10,"en":"Keep DMSO away from heat and contamination, and label it clearly.","nl":"Bewaar DMSO weg van warmte en vervuiling en label het duidelijk."},{"t":"What DMSO Is – Properties & How It Works","tn":"Wat DMSO is – eigenschappen & werking","c":10,"en":"An introduction to what DMSO is and why it behaves uniquely with water and the skin.","nl":"Introductie over wat DMSO is en waarom het zich bijzonder gedraagt met water en de huid.","d":["DMSO (dimethyl sulfoxide) is a highly polar organic solvent derived from wood pulp processing. It is completely colourless and has a mild characteristic scent.","WATER-BINDING: DMSO has a strong natural attraction to water molecules. It pulls water toward application areas, influences cellular hydration, and alters the structure of water around cells — this is why researchers remain interested in its effects on tissue comfort and recovery.","DUAL COMPATIBILITY: DMSO blends easily with both water-rich tissues and lipid layers, allowing it to travel from the skin surface into deeper tissue layers that topical creams rarely access.","TISSUE ENVIRONMENT MODULATOR: DMSO affects the local redox balance, supports natural fluid movement, influences how tissues respond to stress, and alters the transport of certain molecules. It acts more like a biological facilitator than a traditional drug.","NERVE PERCEPTION: Some individuals notice areas treated with DMSO feel warmer, calmer, or lighter. This reflects DMSO's interaction with nerve endings near the skin and local fluid dynamics — not numbing, but a modulation of how nerves perceive their environment.","NORMAL SENSATIONS: Mild warmth, light tingling, slight tightening as the blend dries, a cooling effect from roll-on application, and quick absorption are all normal and expected reactions."],"fr":"Reference information — no specific application frequency"},{"t":"When to Avoid DMSO – Contraindications & Cautions","tn":"Wanneer je DMSO beter vermijdt – contra-indicaties & waarschuwingen","c":10,"en":"Lists situations where DMSO should be paused or avoided, such as damaged skin or recent procedures.","nl":"Somt situaties op waarin je DMSO beter stopt of vermijdt, zoals beschadigde huid of een recente ingreep.","d":["COMPROMISED SKIN BARRIER: Do not apply over open wounds, bleeding or raw areas, severe rashes, burns that have not begun to close, or sites of active infection. Wait until the barrier has stabilised.","RECENT PRODUCT APPLICATION: If lotions, sunscreens, deodorants, makeup, topical medications, or scented products were recently applied, wash thoroughly and let the skin fully reset before using DMSO.","CONTAMINATED ENVIRONMENT: Avoid application near perfumes, hairsprays, cleaning chemicals, diffused essential oils, smoke, or other airborne substances. Gyms, salons, public bathrooms, and recently cleaned rooms are rarely ideal.","INDIVIDUAL SENSITIVITY: People with known sensitivities to sulfur-containing compounds, sulfonamides, or chemical solvents should proceed with caution or avoid DMSO entirely.","PREGNANCY & BREASTFEEDING: Avoid DMSO use during pregnancy or while nursing unless guided by a qualified healthcare professional. Research in these stages is limited.","CONCURRENT PHARMACEUTICALS: Do not layer DMSO over areas treated with topical steroids, hormone creams, prescription ointments, medicated patches, or transdermal drug systems — DMSO can change how these medications are absorbed in unpredictable ways.","MENTAL STATE: If you are rushed, distracted, stressed, or multitasking and cannot protect the area for the necessary settling time, wait. Safe use depends on presence.","UNKNOWN FORMULATIONS: Never use a DMSO formulation if you don't know exactly what's in it. Unlabelled bottles, blends mixed by others, or products from unverified sources undermine safe use.","CLARITY OF PURPOSE: If you're unsure why you're using DMSO — what area you're supporting, what sensation to expect — pause. Intention shapes everything from dilution choice to how you interpret sensations."],"fr":"Review before starting any new DMSO application or changing your routine"}]};
